window.EPISODES = [{"ep":1,"title":"The old monk and the bead","summary":"In Grass Temple Village, Zhang Xiaofan challenges his friend Lin Jingyu for the 98th time, loses again and refuses to give up until he collapses. A wandering monk, Pu Zhi of Tian Yin Temple, saves him and says he has a good foundation. That night Pu Zhi fights a poison cultivator with a Seven-tail Centipede who wants an evil object Pu Zhi carries, and then a masked attacker who uses the Qingyun Sect's Mighty Sword of Thunder. Badly hurt, Pu Zhi takes a Three-day Death Pill and decides to send the two boys to learn at Qingyun. He secretly teaches Xiaofan a breathing method, the Great Brahma Prajna, on strict conditions: tell no one, practise only at night, and use it only to save his life. He gives Xiaofan a bead to throw off a cliff one day, tells him to seek the Ghost Doctor if his life is in danger, and has the boy call him master. Next morning Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu wake under a tree at the village entrance and find the village strange and Mr. Wang raving about ghosts.","events":["Zhang Xiaofan loses to Lin Jingyu for the 98th time and won't admit defeat","Pu Zhi of Tian Yin Temple saves Xiaofan after he collapses","Pu Zhi fights a poison cultivator who wants the evil object he carries","A masked attacker uses the Qingyun Mighty Sword of Thunder against Pu Zhi","Pu Zhi takes a Three-day Death Pill and plans to send the boys to Qingyun","Pu Zhi teaches Xiaofan the Great Brahma Prajna in secret and gives him a bead","The boys wake under a tree at the village entrance; Mr. Wang raves about ghosts"],"introduced":["Zhang Xiaofan","Lin Jingyu","Pu Zhi (Tian Yin Temple monk)","Grass Temple Village","Tian Yin Temple","Qingyun Sect","Great Brahma Prajna","Mighty Sword of Thunder","Seven-tail Centipede","Three-day Death Pill","Ghost Doctor (named only)","the bead Pu Zhi gives Xiaofan"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":2,"title":"Orphans of Qingyun","summary":"Zhang Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu find their parents and their whole village dead. Xiao Yicai brings them up to the Qingyun Sect, where the Water Qilin, tamed by Master Qingye a thousand years ago, roars at them. Sect leader Dao Xuan reports that all 42 households of Grass Temple Village were killed and only three people survived. Questioned, Lin Jingyu says they woke under the tree at the village entrance, and Xiaofan stays silent to keep his promise to Pu Zhi. The peak masters argue over the boys: Cang Song gets Lin Jingyu for Dragon Head Peak, and Xiaofan goes to Tian Buyi's Great Bamboo Peak, which has only seven disciples. Song Daren takes Xiaofan home, Tian Ling'er stops the brothers from teasing him, and Tian Buyi and his wife welcome him over dinner. Xiaofan meets the dog Dahuang, practises Pu Zhi's method at night, and starts the peak's rule for new disciples: cutting the hard black bamboo every day.","events":["Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu grieve in the ruined village","Xiao Yicai brings them to Qingyun; the Water Qilin roars","Dao Xuan reports 42 households killed and three survivors","The peak masters divide the boys: Lin Jingyu to Cang Song, Xiaofan to Tian Buyi","Song Daren brings Xiaofan to Great Bamboo Peak; Tian Ling'er defends him","Xiaofan meets his seniors, serves tea to Tian Buyi and his wife, and is welcomed","Xiaofan practises in secret at night and meets Dahuang","Song Daren starts Xiaofan cutting black bamboo; Du Bishu leaves the peak"],"introduced":["Xiao Yicai (Tongtian Peak)","Water Qilin (called 'Master of Spirit')","Master Qingye (named only)","Dao Xuan (sect leader of Qingyun)","Cang Song (Dragon Head Peak)","Tian Buyi (Great Bamboo Peak)","Shui Yue (Small Bamboo Peak)","Zeng Shucang (Wind Return Peak)","Shang Zhengliang (Morning Sun Peak)","Tian Yun (Falling Rain Peak)","Song Daren, Zheng Dali, Lu Daxin, He Dayi, Wu Dayi, Du Bishu (Great Bamboo Peak disciples)","Tian Ling'er","Su Ru (Tian Buyi's wife, not named yet)","Dahuang","Yuqing Hall, Shoujing Hall","black bamboo of Great Bamboo Peak"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":3,"title":"Slow progress and the thieving monkey","summary":"Years pass and Zhang Xiaofan still makes slow progress on Great Bamboo Peak. Tian Buyi thinks he lacks determination and wishes he were steady like bamboo, and soon after Xiaofan finally breaks through the first level, to his seniors' delight, though Tian Buyi only tells him to go and cook. On Dragon Head Peak, Lin Jingyu has reached the sixth level of the Taiji Xuanqing method after five years, taught by Cang Song himself. Fang Chao challenges him and is nearly killed, and senior disciple Qi Hao scolds Fang Chao for looking down on his junior. Back on Great Bamboo Peak, Xiaofan has become the peak's cook, and a monkey keeps stealing his food. Tian Ling'er chases it with him into an unknown part of the mountain, where Xiaofan loses all his strength and finds her unconscious. He then sees something strange.","events":["Xiaofan still struggles after years on Great Bamboo Peak","Tian Buyi talks of bamboo; Xiaofan breaks through the first level","Lin Jingyu, at the sixth level after five years, nearly kills Fang Chao in a sparring match","Qi Hao scolds Fang Chao and praises Lin Jingyu","A monkey steals Xiaofan's cooking; Tian Ling'er chases it with him","In an unknown place Xiaofan loses his strength and finds Ling'er unconscious"],"introduced":["Fang Chao (Dragon Head Peak)","Qi Hao (Dragon Head Peak)","the grey monkey (Xiao Hui, named in EP4)","Taiji Xuanqing method (Qingyun's cultivation method)"],"cultivation":"Xiaofan breaks through the first level ('Do it for 36 celestial circuits. It's the key of the First Method'). Lin Jingyu 'mastered the sixth level of Qing Method of Taijixuan' after five years (the stage name Yuqing is not said).","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":4,"title":"Xiao Hui and the visitors from Dragon Head Peak","summary":"Zhang Xiaofan wakes after heavy blood loss, and Tian Buyi scolds him and Tian Ling'er for being beaten by a wild monkey. When the monkey turns up again, Ling'er sets Dahuang on it, but Xiaofan shields it and keeps it, naming it Xiao Hui. At night he keeps practising in secret, and his Qingyun qi still clashes with the Brahma Prajna, though it is improving. On Dragon Head Peak, Cang Song gives Lin Jingyu the Dragon-Slaying Sword and teaches him a supreme Qingyun sword skill. Lin Jingyu and Qi Hao then visit Great Bamboo Peak to tell Tian Buyi and Su Ru that the Seven Meridians Tournament will grow to 64 entrants, nine from each peak. Tian Buyi mocks Cang Song but realises every Great Bamboo disciple can now enter. Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu meet for the first time in five years and fight their 99th duel. Ling'er steps in to defend Xiaofan, and Lin Jingyu turns the Dragon-Slaying Sword on her.","events":["Xiaofan wakes; Tian Buyi scolds the pair for losing to a monkey","Xiaofan saves the monkey from Dahuang and names it Xiao Hui","Xiaofan's secret practice: his qi still clashes with the Brahma Prajna","Cang Song gives Lin Jingyu the Dragon-Slaying Sword and a new sword skill","Lin Jingyu and Qi Hao bring the new tournament rules to Great Bamboo Peak","Qi Hao praises Ling'er; Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu meet again after five years","Their 99th duel; Ling'er joins in and Lin Jingyu attacks her with the Dragon-Slaying Sword"],"introduced":["Xiao Hui (the grey monkey, named)","Dragon-Slaying Sword (Lin Jingyu's sword)","Seven Meridians Tournament (called the 'Duel of Seven Ranges')","Su Ru (named as 'Madam Su')"],"cultivation":"Qi Hao says Tian Ling'er 'has mastered the sixth level of Qing Method of Taijixuan' (Taiji Xuanqing, sixth level). Xiaofan's inner thoughts: his qi clashes with the Brahma Prajna at the same stage each time, but he is improving.","confidence":"high"},{"ep":5,"title":"Level three and the road to the tournament","summary":"Tian Buyi and Su Ru stop the fight between Lin Jingyu and Tian Ling'er. Qi Hao apologises for his junior and gives Ling'er a cooling pearl, which she accepts. Lin Jingyu and Zhang Xiaofan promise to do their best at the Seven Meridians Tournament, held every 60 years, and make Grass Temple Village proud. That night Ling'er gives Xiaofan her own copy of the third level of the Taiji Xuanqing method and tells him not to be bullied again; he practises it and finds its qi flows smoothly and feels like the Brahma Prajna. Du Bishu comes back after six years with his Godwood Dice, a flying treasure. On Dragon Head Peak, Lin Jingyu masters a powerful Dragon-Slaying Sword move, and Cang Song, in the hall of ancestral tablets, insists good and evil must be kept apart and he wants the cleanest world. Great Bamboo Peak sets off for the tournament. Xiaofan brings a black stick instead of a sword, rides with Song Daren, falls off on the way, and arrives with the others at the gathering.","events":["Tian Buyi and Su Ru end the fight; Qi Hao apologises and gives Ling'er a cooling pearl","Xiaofan and Lin Jingyu promise to do their best at the tournament","Ling'er gives Xiaofan a copy of the third level; he practises it in secret","Du Bishu returns after six years with the Godwood Dice","Lin Jingyu masters 'Destructive Dashing Dragon'; Cang Song praises him","Cang Song in the ancestral hall: good and evil must stay apart","Great Bamboo Peak flies to the tournament; Xiaofan brings a black stick and falls off on the way"],"introduced":["cooling pearl (Qi Hao's gift to Ling'er)","Godwood Dice (Du Bishu's flying treasure)","Destructive Dashing Dragon (Dragon-Slaying Sword move)","Qi Hao's Ice Sword (named only)","the black stick (Xiaofan's weapon)","hall of the ancestral masters' tablets"],"cultivation":"Xiaofan practises the third level of the Taiji Xuanqing method from Ling'er's copy ('This real Qi of level three met no obstruction'); its qi feels like the Brahma Prajna.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":6,"title":"The tournament opens","summary":"Qingyun's leaders discuss the Blood-Refining Hall, which once stood in the Ten Thousand Bats Cave on Kongsang Mountain 800 years ago and is now stirring again. They decide to ask Fen Xiang Valley and Tian Yin Temple for help and to send the tournament's semi-finalists to scout the cave. At the tournament, Wen Min of Small Bamboo Peak teases Song Daren, and Qi Hao greets Tian Ling'er. Zeng Shushu of Wind Return Peak is fascinated by Xiao Hui, a rare three-eyed monkey that has never been tamed, and befriends Zhang Xiaofan. After the sword ceremony the Water Qilin appears, and the prize is announced: the Liuhe Mirror of the tenth sect leader, Wufangzi. Xiaofan draws number one and goes through the first round because number 64 is missing. Ling'er beats Shen Tiandou of Morning Sun Peak with her Amber Red Twill after he attacks her early. Xiaofan seems distracted, and Zeng Shushu drags him off to watch Lu Xueqi of Small Bamboo Peak.","events":["Qingyun's leaders plan to scout the Ten Thousand Bats Cave with the semi-finalists","Wen Min teases Song Daren; Qi Hao greets Ling'er","Zeng Shushu meets Xiaofan and admires the three-eyed monkey Xiao Hui","Sword ceremony; the Water Qilin appears; the Liuhe Mirror is the prize","Xiaofan draws number one and gets a bye","Ling'er beats Shen Tiandou with the Amber Red Twill","Zeng Shushu gives Xiaofan a rare book and drags him off to see Lu Xueqi"],"introduced":["Blood-Refining Hall (called 'Lianxue Sect')","Ten Thousand Bats Cave (called 'Wanfu Ancient Cave') on Kongsang Mountain","Fen Xiang Valley (named only)","Wen Min (Small Bamboo Peak)","Zeng Shushu (Wind Return Peak)","three-eyed monkey (Xiao Hui's kind)","sword ceremony","Liuhe Mirror (tournament prize)","Wufangzi, Qingyun's tenth sect leader (named only)","Shen Tiandou (Morning Sun Peak)","Amber Red Twill (Ling'er's weapon)","Tianxiang Record (Zeng Shushu's book)","Lu Xueqi (Small Bamboo Peak)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":7,"title":"The Fire Stick's first win","summary":"Lu Xueqi of Small Bamboo Peak beats Fang Chao of Dragon Head Peak and wrecks his sword. An elder asks Shui Yue why her disciple was so ruthless, and Shui Yue answers that he simply wasn't skilled enough; she has given Lu Xueqi the Tianya sword. That night Zhang Xiaofan and Tian Ling'er slip out in secret. Next day Xiaofan faces Chu Yuhong of Morning Sun Peak, a favourite, using the black stick he calls the Fire Stick. Chu Yuhong sees that Xiaofan has reached Yuqing level 4 (Jade Purity), and Xiaofan wins and reaches the top 16. Du Bishu, the only one who bet on Xiaofan, collects his winnings, and Tian Buyi warns his disciples against arrogance and tells Xiaofan he will face Lu Xueqi. Zeng Shushu arranges for his peak-mate Peng Chang to go easy on Xiaofan, and Xiaofan remembers Tian Buyi and Su Ru training him. In the match, Peng Chang is offended that Xiaofan has wrapped his weapon and attacks him for real.","events":["Lu Xueqi beats Fang Chao and breaks his sword; Shui Yue defends her","The draw pairs Xiaofan with Chu Yuhong; Xiaofan and Ling'er slip out at night","Xiaofan beats Chu Yuhong with the Fire Stick and reaches the top 16","Du Bishu wins his bet; Tian Buyi warns against arrogance","Zeng Shushu asks Peng Chang to go easy on Xiaofan","Xiaofan remembers Tian Buyi and Su Ru training him","Peng Chang takes offence at the wrapped stick and fights seriously"],"introduced":["Tianya (Lu Xueqi's sword, named only)","Chu Yuhong (Morning Sun Peak)","Fire Stick (Xiaofan's name for his black stick, 'Fire Burning Stick')","Peng Chang (Wind Return Peak)","the small yellow pill (Great Bamboo Peak medicine)","Yuwu skill (controlling a weapon with qi)"],"cultivation":"Chu Yuhong to Xiaofan: 'You've mastered Quwu to the fourth level of Yuqing' (Yuqing level 4). Ling'er is said to have mastered the Yuwu skill, driving her Amber Red Twill with qi.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":8,"title":"Lu Xueqi's thunder","summary":"Lu Xueqi beats Tian Ling'er, who was distracted by Qi Hao cheering her on, and goes into the top eight. Zhang Xiaofan comes back badly hurt but has beaten Peng Chang and is also in the top eight. Tian Buyi sees that Xiaofan's Taiji Xuanqing is at the fourth level, not the second, and suspects Ling'er of teaching him in secret. He and Su Ru argue about Ling'er, who has fallen for Qi Hao, a Dragon Head Peak disciple Tian Buyi can't stand; alone, Ling'er swears she and Qi Hao will be together forever. With Song Daren and Chang Jian badly injured, Xiaofan is the last Great Bamboo Peak disciple left, and he faces Lu Xueqi before he has recovered. Lu Xueqi calls down the Mighty Sword of Thunder despite a warning that it could backfire, and Xiaofan, expecting to die, wonders if Ling'er will remember him. Lu Xueqi wins. An elder then tells Dao Xuan that Xiaofan, only at Yuqing level 4 (Jade Purity), has a weapon that rivals Tianya and seems refined with blood, and that it does not belong to Qingyun.","events":["Lu Xueqi beats Tian Ling'er and reaches the top eight","Xiaofan, badly hurt, has beaten Peng Chang and is in the top eight","Tian Buyi finds Xiaofan at the fourth level and suspects Ling'er","Tian Buyi and Su Ru argue about Ling'er and Qi Hao; Ling'er swears to stay with Qi Hao","Xiaofan faces Lu Xueqi in the top-eight round","Lu Xueqi uses the Mighty Sword of Thunder and wins","An elder warns Dao Xuan that Xiaofan's weapon is evil and blood-refined"],"introduced":["Tianya Divine Sword (Lu Xueqi's sword, seen in use)","Chang Jian (a top-eight contestant, named only)"],"cultivation":"Tian Buyi: Xiaofan 'should've mastered only the second level of Qing Method of Taijixuan. Why is it at the fourth level?' An elder to Dao Xuan: 'He only mastered the fourth level of Yuqing, yet he has a weapon that rivals Tianya' (Yuqing level 4).","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":9,"title":"Down the mountain to Heyang","summary":"Cang Song accuses Zhang Xiaofan of being a Demon Sect spy because his stick is refined with blood, and demands he be beheaded under Qingyun's rules, while Tian Buyi defends him. Dao Xuan rules that the weapon does not look like a Demon Sect weapon and tells Cang Song that Qingyun must not kill the innocent. Xiaofan placed fourth in the tournament, so Dao Xuan sends him down the mountain with the top disciples and returns the stick, saying only he can use it. Xiaofan, who has only just learned to fly, flies with Qi Hao, Lu Xueqi and Zeng Shushu to Heyang, the biggest city in the Central Plain. At the Shanhai Garden restaurant a girl named Bi Yao mocks their signature sleeping fish and says Qingyun does nothing but farm fish. That night Lu Xueqi asks Xiaofan why he gave up at the last moment of their match, and he insists he simply wasn't good enough. Later, woken by a nightmare, Xiaofan finds Bi Yao plucking a flower in the garden; they argue over whether dew is the flower's tears, and he tells her his name.","events":["Cang Song calls Xiaofan a Demon Sect spy and wants him beheaded; Tian Buyi defends him","Dao Xuan clears Xiaofan, returns the stick, and notes he placed fourth","Dao Xuan sends Xiaofan down the mountain with the top disciples","Xiaofan, Qi Hao, Lu Xueqi and Zeng Shushu fly to Heyang","At Shanhai Garden, Bi Yao mocks the sleeping fish and Qingyun","Lu Xueqi asks Xiaofan why he gave up at the end of their match","Xiaofan meets Bi Yao at night over a plucked flower and tells her his name"],"introduced":["Bi Yao","Heyang (city near Qingyun)","Shanhai Garden (restaurant in Heyang)","sleeping fish (raised in Qingyun's Hong River)","Zhugou Mountain (named only)"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":10,"title":"Kongsang Mountain and the Blood-Refining Hall","summary":"In Heyang, Bi Yao tells You Ji that the Qingyun group is led by Qi Hao and that one of them is Zhang Xiaofan, and she grieves over her mother, who named her weapon Sad Flower. You Ji reminds her that their own trip to Kongsang Mountain matters. After ten days of flying, Qi Hao, Zeng Shushu, Lu Xueqi and Zhang Xiaofan are attacked by Blood Bats outside the Ten Thousand Bats Cave. Fa Xiang of Tian Yin Temple drives the bats off with his Liuhe Mirror, and he, Fa Shan, Li Xun and Yan Hong of Fen Xiang Valley join them inside. In the cave the Blood-Refining Hall survivors Ye Gou Daoren, Nian Laoda and the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect's Jiang Laosan ambush them. Jiang Laosan grabs Zhang Xiaofan and ends up drained dry by his stick, which Nian Laoda takes for a blood-sucking skill; Xiaofan does not know what happened. The group chases the demons to the Abyss of the Dead, where Xiao Zhou, Lin Feng and the rest of the Hall wait, and the episode ends with Lu Xueqi caught by a binding spell.","events":["Bi Yao and You Ji talk about the Qingyun group, her mother and the Sad Flower","Blood Bats attack the Qingyun group at the Ten Thousand Bats Cave on Kongsang Mountain","Fa Xiang's Liuhe Mirror drives off the bats; Tian Yin Temple and Fen Xiang Valley join Qingyun","Ye Gou Daoren, Jiang Laosan and Nian Laoda ambush them in the cave","Jiang Laosan dies after Zhang Xiaofan's stick drains his blood; the demons flee","The chase ends at the Abyss of the Dead, the Blood-Refining Hall's forbidden ground","Xiao Zhou, Lin Feng and the Hall fight the young disciples; Lu Xueqi is bound"],"introduced":["You Ji (called Aunt You by Bi Yao)","Sad Flower (Bi Yao's weapon, named by her mother)","Huqi Mountain","Kongsang Mountain and the Ten Thousand Bats Cave (Wanfu Ancient Cave)","Blood Bats","Fa Xiang and Fa Shan (Tian Yin Temple)","Li Xun and Yan Hong (Fen Xiang Valley)","Liuhe Mirror (Fa Xiang's treasure)","Ye Gou Daoren, Nian Laoda, Xiao Zhou, Lin Feng (Blood-Refining Hall)","Jiang Laosan (Ten Thousand Poisons Sect)","Abyss of the Dead (Siling Abyss)","Shanhe Fan"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":11,"title":"Falling into the Abyss of the Dead","summary":"At the Abyss of the Dead, Lin Feng holds Lu Xueqi with a binding spell until Zhang Xiaofan frees her. Nian Laoda unleashes his Red Devil Eyes, which suppress Lu Xueqi's Tianxie Sword, but Xiaofan's stick holds it back. Nian Laoda knocks Xiaofan over the edge; Lu Xueqi catches his hand, refuses to let go, and both fall into the abyss. Fen Xiang and Tian Yin reinforcements destroy the Hall's weapon forge, and the Blood-Refining Hall pulls back, saying two righteous disciples are dead. At the bottom, Lu Xueqi finds herself in a sealed cave with the badly hurt Xiaofan and fights off creatures until she collapses. Xiaofan wakes and heals her. Bi Yao and You Ji then arrive looking for the Dixue Cave, decide to take the two captive for the Ghost King's side, and the episode ends as something huge appears.","events":["Zhang Xiaofan frees Lu Xueqi from Lin Feng's binding","Nian Laoda's Red Devil Eyes suppress the Tianxie Sword; Xiaofan's stick resists it","Xiaofan is knocked into the abyss; Lu Xueqi holds his hand and falls with him","Reinforcements destroy the Hall's forge; the Blood-Refining Hall retreats","Lu Xueqi wakes in a sealed cave and fights off creatures to protect Xiaofan","Xiaofan wakes and heals Lu Xueqi","Bi Yao and You Ji arrive searching for the Dixue Cave and move to capture them"],"introduced":["Red Devil Eyes (Nian Laoda's treasure)","Tianxie Sword (Lu Xueqi's sword)","Dixue Cave (Black Heart Elder's hidden cave)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":12,"title":"Trapped with Bi Yao in the Dixue Cave","summary":"A Black Water Snake attacks, and Zhang Xiaofan draws it away so Lu Xueqi can escape. Bi Yao saves him, and the two end up trapped together in the snake's tunnels while Lu Xueqi rejoins Qi Hao and the others. Xiaofan has a broken bone and calls Bi Yao a devil; they bicker and wander the dead-end tunnels until he notices a bleeding rock. It opens into the Dixue Cave, where they find the corpse of Black Heart Elder, the Blood-Refining Hall master of 800 years ago, but no treasure. Xiaofan falls into a fever and relives the massacre of his village, and Bi Yao learns he is an orphan and keeps him warm. Outside, the search party finds nothing after many days; Lu Xueqi wants to keep looking, but the others decide to go back and ask the sect leader for trackers. Xiaofan recovers, a skull falls and opens a hidden passage, and they find a poem of regret and the statues of the Wisdom King and the Holy Mother.","events":["The Black Water Snake attacks; Zhang Xiaofan draws it away from Lu Xueqi","Bi Yao saves Xiaofan; the two are trapped together","Lu Xueqi rejoins the others; they search for Xiaofan","A bleeding rock leads to the Dixue Cave and Black Heart Elder's corpse","Xiaofan's fever and nightmare of the village massacre; Bi Yao cares for him","The search party decides to report back to Qingyun; Lu Xueqi is persuaded to go","A hidden passage opens onto a poem and the statues of the Wisdom King and the Holy Mother"],"introduced":["Black Water Snake","Black Heart Elder (Black-Hearted Old Man), master of the Blood-Refining Hall 800 years ago","Ancient Corpse Poison","Sinister Bead (named here the Blood-Striking Bead)","Wisdom King and Holy Mother (statues revered by the Demon Sect)"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":13,"title":"The Hehuan Bell and the Heavenly Book","summary":"Bi Yao bows to the Wisdom King and the Holy Mother as a 43rd-generation disciple. Behind Ancient Corpse Poison, Black Heart Elder had hidden only a pair of bells: the Hehuan Bell of Madam Jinling, founder of the He Huan Sect. Bi Yao explains that Jinling and Black Heart Elder were lovers from rival sects 800 years ago. Ghost fire then reveals carvings of the Heavenly Book, the Demon Sect's classic, and Zhang Xiaofan is shaken to find lines from the Great Brahma Prajna and the Taiji Xuanqing Dao in it. With the food gone, Bi Yao asks him to kill her and eat her so he can live, then tries to kill herself. When he stops her, she tells him how she and her mother were buried in a cave by the Tian Yin monk Pu Fang, how her mother fed her until she died, and how her father seemed to want to kill her when he came. She prays with her own blood to send Xiaofan home to Great Bamboo Peak. That sets off the Lovestruck Mantra, which opens the exit. They escape as the cave collapses, and Xiaofan cooks her a meal.","events":["Bi Yao bows to the statues as a 43rd-generation disciple","The Hehuan Bell of Madam Jinling is found behind Ancient Corpse Poison","Bi Yao tells the story of Madam Jinling and Black Heart Elder","The Heavenly Book carvings echo Tian Yin and Qingyun teachings, shaking Zhang Xiaofan","Bi Yao asks Xiaofan to eat her, then tries to kill herself","Bi Yao tells how her mother died in Liuhu Cave","Her blood prayer triggers the Lovestruck Mantra; the exit opens and they escape"],"introduced":["Hehuan Bell (a pair of bells)","Madam Jinling, founder of the He Huan Sect","He Huan Sect","Heavenly Book","Pu Fang (Tian Yin monk who buried Bi Yao's family)","Liuhu Cave","Lovestruck Mantra (a women-only mantra deciphered from the Heavenly Book)"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":14,"title":"Wan Renwang at the tea stall","summary":"Out of the cave, Bi Yao asks Zhang Xiaofan to repay her by joining her sect; they argue over which side is sinful, and she leaves in anger. On Small Bamboo Peak, Shui Yue scolds Lu Xueqi for losing focus. At a roadside tea stall an old man calling himself Wan Renwang tells Xiaofan that the bead on his stick is Black Heart Elder's Blood-Striking Bead and that the stick is a demonic weapon. Xiaofan answers that he uses it to kill demons, so it is righteous, and the man vanishes. The man is the Ghost King: he meets Bi Yao, shows her the flower her mother gave him, takes her home, and plans to win Xiaofan over once the weapon has turned him into a killer. Xiaofan reaches a deserted town afraid of a Three-Tailed Fox. A fortune teller with a young granddaughter reads his face, warns that he is close to death, and takes four taels. Shi Tou, heir of the Jingang Sect, wants to kill the fox, and Xiaofan goes with him to the Black Stone Cave.","events":["Bi Yao asks Zhang Xiaofan to join her sect; they argue and part angrily","Shui Yue scolds Lu Xueqi for losing focus","Wan Renwang names the Blood-Striking Bead and calls the stick demonic; Xiaofan refuses to doubt it","The Ghost King takes Bi Yao home and they make up over her mother's flower","The Ghost King plans to bring Xiaofan to his side","A town fears the Three-Tailed Fox; a fortune teller reads Xiaofan's face","Shi Tou of the Jingang Sect and Xiaofan set out for the Black Stone Cave"],"introduced":["Ghost King (calls himself Wan Renwang)","Blood-Striking Bead (the Sinister Bead)","Jiuyou Soul; the stick named 'Dementor' in an ancient book","Zhu Xian Sword (mentioned)","Three-Tailed Fox","Zhou Yixian (the fortune teller, unnamed here) and his granddaughter","Shi Tou, only successor of Master Dali of the Jingang Sect","Black Stone Cave (Heishi Cave)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":15,"title":"The Three-Tailed Fox at the ancient well","summary":"Zhang Xiaofan and Shi Tou cross a misty forest, where Shi Tou shows off his Aura Breaker and says the Jingang Sect is related to Tian Yin Temple. They find a woman singing by a 3,000-year-old well: she is the Three-Tailed Fox, who prays there to cure her sick big brother. She tempts Xiaofan to look into the well, and someone steps in to stop the fight. Li Xun and Yan Hong of Fen Xiang Valley arrive and say the Six-Tailed Fox stole their Red Fire Mirror; the Three-Tailed Fox says Shangguan of Fen Xiang injured her brother. She lures them into the Black Stone Cave. Bi Yao follows Xiaofan in, and Shi Tou is glad of her help. A dragon-like beast rises from the ground, Xiaofan falls during the fight, and he steadies himself with a Buddhist chant. Below, he meets the Six-Tailed Fox.","events":["Shi Tou shows his Aura Breaker in the misty forest","The Three-Tailed Fox sings by the ancient well and tempts Xiaofan to look in","Li Xun and Yan Hong arrive hunting the fox for Fen Xiang's Red Fire Mirror","The fox lures everyone into the Black Stone Cave","Bi Yao follows Xiaofan in; a beast rises from the ground","Xiaofan falls and calms himself with a Buddhist chant","Xiaofan meets the Six-Tailed Fox"],"introduced":["Aura Breaker (Shi Tou's weapon)","The 3,000-year-old ancient well (Full Moon Ancient Well)","Six-Tailed Fox","Red Fire Mirror (Fen Xiang Valley's stolen treasure)","Shangguan (a Fen Xiang elder, mentioned)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":16,"title":"The two foxes","summary":"Below the Black Stone Cave, Zhang Xiaofan tells the Six-Tailed Fox he has come to kill him for harming the villagers. The fox answers that greedy humans woke the beast in the cave, and that the foxes have been holding it back. Shi Tou fights the beast with his Aura Breaker. The Six-Tailed Fox is dying of Jiuhan Ice poison that ruined nearly 1,000 years of training. With Fen Xiang Valley closing in after 300 years, he begs the Three-Tailed Fox to escape, but she refuses to leave him and gives her life. He asks for her song once more, gives Xiaofan the Red Fire Mirror and tells him to keep it hidden, and the two foxes die together. When Li Xun asks, Xiaofan says he did not see the mirror. Yan Hong tells him Qingyun is meeting the other righteous sects at Liubo Mountain in the East Sea, and Xiaofan, Shi Tou and Bi Yao head back to tell the village the foxes are dead.","events":["The Six-Tailed Fox argues that humans, not foxes, stirred up the cave","Shi Tou fights the beast with his Aura Breaker","The Six-Tailed Fox is dying of Jiuhan Ice poison and begs the Three-Tailed Fox to flee","The Three-Tailed Fox gives her life rather than leave him","The Six-Tailed Fox gives Xiaofan the Red Fire Mirror and dies with her","Xiaofan hides the mirror from Li Xun","Yan Hong points Xiaofan to Liubo Mountain"],"introduced":["Jiuhan Ice poison","Huqi Mountain (where the foxes met)","Full Moon Ancient Well","Liubo Mountain in the East Sea (mentioned)"],"cultivation":"The Six-Tailed Fox says nearly 1,000 years of training were ruined by the Jiuhan Ice poison; the Three-Tailed Fox has trained for 300 years.","confidence":"high"},{"ep":17,"title":"Back to Great Bamboo Peak's family","summary":"The villagers cheer Zhang Xiaofan, Shi Tou and Bi Yao for ending the fox trouble, and Bi Yao warns them to stay away from the Black Stone Cave. Xiaofan asks the fortune teller whether demons have feelings, and the old man says there are good demons and bad people. At the Haiyun Building inn in Changhe, Bi Yao tells Xiaofan she half wishes they had died in the Dixue Cave and asks whether the line between the Demon Sect and the righteous matters so much to him. He cannot answer, and she leaves in the night with You Ji, having paid his bill. Shi Tou is called home to the Jingang Sect. Flying alone over the sea to Liubo Mountain, Xiaofan is attacked by Nian Laoda, Ye Gou Daoren and the Blood-Refining Hall. Tian Ling'er, Song Daren and Du Bishu come to help, and Tian Buyi's arrival drives the demons off. Xiaofan is welcomed back by Su Ru and Lin Jingyu, then learns that Tian Ling'er and Qi Hao are engaged.","events":["The village celebrates; Bi Yao warns them off the Black Stone Cave","The fortune teller answers Xiaofan's question about demons","Bi Yao's night talk with Xiaofan at the Haiyun Building; she leaves with You Ji","Shi Tou returns to the Jingang Sect","The Blood-Refining Hall attacks Xiaofan over the sea near Liubo Mountain","Tian Ling'er, Song Daren, Du Bishu and then Tian Buyi rescue him","Reunion with Su Ru and Lin Jingyu; Tian Ling'er and Qi Hao are engaged"],"introduced":["Haiyun Building in Changhe (an inn)","Jingang Sect","Shenmu Dice (a weapon called in the sea fight)","Tusk Sword"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":18,"title":"Kneeling in the rain; the Demon Sect gathers at Liubo Mountain","summary":"A strong evil aura comes off Zhang Xiaofan and he fights Song Daren. Tian Buyi orders him to kneel and repent, and sends Lin Jingyu, who tries to stand by him, back with Qi Hao. Bi Yao slips onto the peak and finds Xiaofan in the rain; she prays to the Wisdom King and the Holy Mother for him, but he insists he deserves punishment. In the morning Tian Buyi tells him that Tian Ling'er loves Qi Hao and sees him only as a younger brother, and gives him a mission. Searching Liubo Mountain with Ling'er, Xiaofan finds a cave where Demon Sect members are waiting for the Kui, a divine beast seen every 3,000 years, and are demanding the Ghost King explain himself. Bi Yao speaks for her father; Baiduzi and Elder Duanmu of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect argue about whether to stay. Bi Yao exposes a man sowing discord as a Qingyun spy by his Taiji Xuanqing Dao and Seven Star Sword. Xiaofan and Ling'er jump in to help him, and he turns out to be Xiao Yicai. Bi Yao uses the Hehuan Bell, and the Ghost King appears and warns her that it backfires on the unskilled.","events":["Zhang Xiaofan's evil aura flares and he fights Song Daren","Tian Buyi makes him kneel in the rain; Lin Jingyu is sent away","Bi Yao visits him in the rain and prays for him","Tian Buyi tells him Ling'er sees him as a younger brother and gives him a mission","Xiaofan and Ling'er find the Demon Sect waiting for the Kui on Liubo Mountain","Bi Yao exposes a Qingyun spy; Xiaofan and Ling'er help him; he is Xiao Yicai","The Ghost King appears and warns Bi Yao about the Hehuan Bell"],"introduced":["Kui (Kui Ox), a divine beast seen every 3,000 years","Baiduzi (Ten Thousand Poisons Sect)","Elder Duanmu (Ten Thousand Poisons Sect)","Longevity Hall (Changsheng Sect, mentioned)","Seven Star Sword (a Qingyun technique)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":19,"title":"The Ghost King's offer and Master Xixue","summary":"On Liubo Mountain the Ghost King greets Zhang Xiaofan as an old acquaintance: he was the tea-stall owner Wan Renwang who approached Xiaofan after Kongsang Mountain. Bi Yao fights Tian Ling'er, then the Ghost King lets the Qingyun disciples go for his daughter's sake, because Xiaofan went through the Abyss of the Dead with her and got her to forgive her father. He invites Xiaofan to join his sect and marry Bi Yao, and Xiaofan says he would rather die. Xiao Yicai reports that the Demon Sect is gathering on Liubo Mountain to hunt the Kui Ox; Cang Song wants to strike at once, Tian Buyi agrees that Great Bamboo Peak never backs down, and the Tian Yin Temple monks join in. In private Xiao Yicai tells Tian Buyi that Xiaofan knows Bi Yao and the Ghost King and asks him to keep it from Cang Song, and Su Ru tells her husband he cares more about Xiaofan than he admits. That night Master Xixue of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect attacks Xiaofan to avenge his disciple Jiang Laosan, recognises the power of Xiaofan's stick, and nearly kills him before Tian Buyi steps in.","events":["The Ghost King reveals he was Wan Renwang from the tea stall","Bi Yao fights Tian Ling'er; the Ghost King lets the disciples go and asks Xiaofan to join him","Xiaofan refuses: he would rather die than join the Demon Sect","Xiao Yicai reports the Demon Sect gathering at Liubo Mountain for the Kui Ox; Qingyun and Tian Yin Temple agree to attack in the morning","Xiao Yicai privately tells Tian Buyi about Xiaofan and Bi Yao and asks him to keep it from Cang Song","Su Ru and Tian Buyi talk about Xiaofan","Master Xixue attacks Xiaofan over Jiang Laosan's death; Tian Buyi arrives and confronts him"],"introduced":["Master Xixue (Ten Thousand Poisons Sect; Jiang Laosan's master)","Five Ghost Spirits (Master Xixue's spell)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":20,"title":"The Kui Ox wakes on Liubo Mountain","summary":"Mr. Ghost of the Ghost King Sect performs a blood ritual, offering souls and flesh so the coming beast's thunder can be resisted. Tian Buyi and Cang Song lead the attack but walk into a trap: Baiduzi of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect fills the valley with poison gas, and You Ji, Elder Duanmu, Nian Laoda and Qing Long surround them. In the battle Lin Jingyu fights with the Dragon-Slaying Sword, which startles the demon he faces, and an old enemy of Cang Song comes for revenge. Tian Buyi sees an evil omen over the sea and sends Zhang Xiaofan and the young disciples to look. Their weapons are held by a formation, so Xiaofan, whose stick still works, stays behind to fight, and Lu Xueqi helps him. At the shore the Ghost King binds the newborn Kui Ox with the Dragon-Trapping Que. He tells Xiaofan that if the Kui breaks free its thunder will kill everyone on Liubo Mountain, and asks whether that would make Xiaofan righteous or evil. Xiaofan decides to break the formation anyway.","events":["Mr. Ghost performs a soul-offering ritual","Tian Buyi and Cang Song are ambushed with poison gas by Baiduzi; You Ji, Elder Duanmu, Nian Laoda and Qing Long close in","Lin Jingyu fights with the Dragon-Slaying Sword; an old enemy attacks Cang Song","Tian Buyi sends Xiaofan and the disciples to the sea; a formation holds their weapons and Xiaofan stays behind","Lu Xueqi helps Xiaofan; he thanks her for saving him in the Abyss of the Dead","The Ghost King's followers retreat to the sea; the Kui Ox is born","The Ghost King binds the Kui with the Dragon-Trapping Que and fights Xiaofan","Xiaofan resolves to break the formation"],"introduced":["Mr. Ghost (Ghost King Sect)","Qing Long (Ghost King Sect)","Kui Ox (the divine beast of Liubo Mountain, first seen)","Dragon-Trapping Que (the Ghost King's binding artefact)","Dragon-Slaying Sword (named; Lin Jingyu's sword)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":21,"title":"The Sinister Bead and the Great Brahma Prajna exposed","summary":"Zhang Xiaofan breaks the Ghost King's formation at the sea, and the Ghost King's followers say the chance to take the Kui Ox is lost. In the fight the Sinister Bead on Xiaofan's stick is recognised as the Black-Hearted Old Man's treasure, and Xiaofan uses the Great Brahma Prajna, Tian Yin Temple's secret skill, in front of everyone. The Ghost King still swears to subdue the beast even at the cost of his life, while Bi Yao tries to reach Xiaofan and has to be held back. Afterwards Cang Song demands Xiaofan's death for colluding with the Demon Sect, Tian Buyi refuses to hand him over, and Tian Yin Temple's Fa Xiang and Fa Shan leave to report to their abbot. Xiaofan wakes after three days in an inn at Changhe near the East Sea; Lin Jingyu says he trusts him, but Dragon Head Peak disciples take Xiaofan away for questioning on Cang Song's order. Bi Yao wants to go to him, but You Ji stops her. The leaders of the four demon sects, including the Poison God, San Miao and Yu Yangzi, meet for the first time in a hundred years and swear to rise again.","events":["Xiaofan breaks the formation; the Ghost King's side says the chance is lost","The Sinister Bead is recognised as the Black-Hearted Old Man's; Xiaofan uses the Great Brahma Prajna","The Ghost King vows to subdue the beast even at the cost of his life; Bi Yao tries to reach Xiaofan","Cang Song demands Xiaofan's death; Tian Buyi refuses; Fa Xiang and Fa Shan return to Tian Yin Temple to report","Xiaofan wakes at an inn in Changhe; Lin Jingyu says he trusts him; Dragon Head Peak disciples take him away","Zhou Yixian tells Xiao Huan about the Full Moon Ancient Well","Xiaofan, locked in a room, talks to Xiao Hui; You Ji stops Bi Yao from going to him","The four demon sects gather: the Poison God, San Miao and Yu Yangzi"],"introduced":["Poison God (master of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect)","San Miao (He Huan Sect)","Yu Yangzi (master of the Longevity Hall)","Full Moon Ancient Well (shows the person you love most at full moon)","Wisdom King and Holy Mother (the Demon Sect's revered deities)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":22,"title":"Bi Yao on Qingyun Mountain","summary":"At Yuqing Temple on Tongtian Peak, sect leader Dao Xuan apologises to Pu Hong, abbot of Tian Yin Temple, who says Zhang Xiaofan is young and should be forgiven. Shangguan Ce arrives from Fen Xiang Valley on Yun Yilan's orders, mocks Pu Hong's mercy, and says Fen Xiang's Mystic Fire Mirror is tied to Xiaofan. Cang Song argues that Xiaofan must be punished to save Qingyun's name. In the demon camp the Ghost King asks the Poison God to back his leadership of the alliance, hinting that the Seven-Tailed Centipede is down to its last pair and offering to share the world once Qingyun falls. Song Daren tells Xiaofan that Tian Buyi swore on his life to Dao Xuan and Cang Song that Xiaofan is no spy, and that Xiaofan will be questioned before everyone at Yuqing Temple in the morning. Bi Yao slips onto the mountain and finds Xiaofan in the back hills; she asks him to run away with her, but he says Qingyun is his home and he cannot betray his master and his master's wife. She promises to tell him who she saw in the Full Moon Ancient Well when they meet again. Dao Xuan visits a hidden old man for advice, Bi Yao learns her father has secretly moved his main force to Qingyun Mountain, and the four demon leaders swear to destroy Qingyun.","events":["Dao Xuan receives Pu Hong at Yuqing Temple; Pu Hong argues for mercy","Shangguan Ce of Fen Xiang Valley arrives and links the Mystic Fire Mirror to Xiaofan","The Ghost King presses the Poison God to join him against Qingyun","Song Daren tells Xiaofan that Tian Buyi vouched for him with his life; the trial is set for morning","Bi Yao meets Xiaofan on the back mountain and asks him to leave with her; he refuses","Dao Xuan speaks with a hidden old man about mercy","You Ji tells Bi Yao the Demon Sect's full force is moving on Qingyun","The four demon leaders swear revenge for the Holy Temple a hundred years ago: 'Destroy Qingyun Sect!'"],"introduced":["Pu Hong (abbot of Tian Yin Temple)","Shangguan Ce (Fen Xiang Valley)","Yun Yilan (master of Fen Xiang Valley, named only)","Seven-Tailed Centipede (the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect's beast)","Holy Temple (where five Qingyun disciples crushed the Demon Sect a hundred years ago)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":23,"title":"Zhang Xiaofan on trial","summary":"Qingyun's laws are read out: colluding with the Demon Sect, betraying the sect and killing innocents are punished by death. Mad Wang Er, a survivor of Grass Temple Village, wanders onto Tongtian Peak shouting 'Ghost!', while the Ghost King's forces break Qingyun's protective formation, the Ghost King saying someone taught him how. At Yuqing Temple Dao Xuan questions Zhang Xiaofan: he admits using the Great Brahma Prajna on Liubo Mountain but refuses to say who taught him. Pu Hong argues against a death sentence, while Shangguan Ce and Cang Song accuse Xiaofan of carrying the Sinister Bead and colluding with Bi Yao. Xiaofan says Bi Yao saved his life in Dixue Cave and that he owes her gratitude, but he denies betraying the sect. When Dao Xuan announces the harshest punishment, Lu Xueqi swears on her life that Xiaofan is no traitor, then Lin Jingyu and others do the same. Xiao Yicai reports that the sword formation is broken and intruders are on Tongtian Peak, and Dao Xuan leaves to deal with them. When he returns to pass sentence, Seven-Tailed Centipede poison strikes him, the blame falls on Xiaofan, and a second attacker hits him, crying that this day has finally come, as the Demon Sect storms the mountain.","events":["Qingyun's laws are recited","Mad Wang Er appears on Tongtian Peak shouting 'Ghost!'","The Ghost King's forces break Qingyun's protective formation","Dao Xuan questions Xiaofan; he admits the Great Brahma Prajna but won't name his teacher","Shangguan Ce and Cang Song accuse him over the Sinister Bead and Bi Yao; Pu Hong opposes a death sentence","Lu Xueqi, Lin Jingyu and others swear on their lives that Xiaofan is innocent","The sword formation is broken; Dao Xuan leaves, then returns to pass sentence","Dao Xuan is poisoned by a Seven-Tailed Centipede and attacked; the Demon Sect storms Qingyun"],"introduced":["Wang Er (mad survivor of Grass Temple Village, named)","Asura Tower (destroyed by Qingyun in the past, per the Ghost King)"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":24,"title":"Cang Song's betrayal","summary":"In Yuqing Temple, Cang Song admits he set the trap for Dao Xuan. For a hundred years he has hated Dao Xuan over Wan Jianyi, the man who saved his life, who he says should have led the sect. He calls Tian Buyi a bootlicker, openly sides with the Demon Sect as it breaks in, and Zhang Xiaofan suspects he is the one who massacred Grass Temple Village. Dao Xuan decides to break the ancestors' rule and use the ancient Zhu Xian Sword; Shang Zhengliang, Tian Yun and Shui Yue are told to guard Yuqing Temple with Zeng Shucang, and Tian Buyi goes after Cang Song. Pu Hong is struck down by an ally he trusted, and Zhou Yin of the Longevity Hall tries to ambush Dao Xuan, who escapes and sends the young disciples to guard the paths to Huanyue Cave and the Ancestral Hall. Yu Yangzi attacks Yuqing Temple with his Yin-Yang Mirror, and Tian Buyi fights first Cang Song and then the Ghost King. At the Ancestral Hall an old servant kills Zhou Yin, shows Lin Jingyu how the Dragon-Slaying Sword should really be used, and gives him a message for Dao Xuan; Zhou Yin recognises him as Wan Jianyi just before he dies. Xiaofan, Lu Xueqi and Lin Jingyu regroup as the Zhu Xian Sword rises over Qingyun.","events":["Cang Song admits ambushing Dao Xuan and names his grudge over Wan Jianyi","The Demon Sect breaks in; Cang Song openly sides with it; Xiaofan suspects him of the village massacre","Dao Xuan decides to use the Zhu Xian Sword; the peak masters are posted to guard Yuqing Temple","Pu Hong is struck down by a supposed ally; Zhou Yin tries to ambush Dao Xuan","Yu Yangzi attacks Yuqing Temple with the Yin-Yang Mirror","The Ancestral Hall's old servant kills Zhou Yin and teaches Lin Jingyu the Dragon-Slaying Sword","Tian Buyi fights Cang Song, then the Ghost King","The Zhu Xian Sword appears over Qingyun"],"introduced":["Zhou Yin (Longevity Hall; weapon: Liren Awl)","Yin-Yang Mirror (Yu Yangzi's treasure)","Huanyue Cave and the Ancestral Hall (Qingyun's sacred places)","Zhu Xian Sword (seen)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":25,"title":"The Zhu Xian Sword Formation and Pu Zhi's secret","summary":"Dao Xuan unleashes the Zhu Xian Sword Formation, and the stunned demon leaders wonder whether he has reached Taiqing (Grand Purity); the Demon Sect pulls back. The cost is heavy: of Qingyun's 25 elders, 14 are dead and five badly hurt, Tian Yun and Shang Zhengliang among the dead, and Pu Hong reveals that 'Shangguan Ce' was a Demon Sect impostor who ambushed him. Before the dead, Dao Xuan again asks Zhang Xiaofan for his secret, and Pu Kong of Tian Yin Temple threatens to punish him. Then mad Wang Er points at the bald monk as the 'ghost' who killed the villagers, and Pu Hong confesses that the murderer of Grass Temple Village came from Tian Yin Temple. In the demon camp the leaders blame Cang Song for promising Dao Xuan would not use the sword, learn that Bi Yao is missing on Qingyun, and agree to strike again while Dao Xuan is weak. Pu Hong tells Dao Xuan the full story: Pu Zhi came to Qingyun to propose studying Buddhism and Taoism together and was refused, was wounded by a man in black while guarding the Sinister Bead, and secretly taught Zhang Xiaofan the Great Brahma Prajna. Twisted by the bead and with only days to live, Pu Zhi slaughtered the village himself so Qingyun would have to take in the two boys, then returned to Tian Yin Temple to confess before he died.","events":["Dao Xuan's Zhu Xian Sword Formation drives the Demon Sect back","Qingyun counts its dead: 14 of 25 elders, including Tian Yun and Shang Zhengliang","Pu Hong reveals the fake Shangguan Ce ambushed him","Wang Er identifies a bald monk as the village killer; Pu Hong confesses that the killer came from Tian Yin Temple","The demon leaders turn on Cang Song, learn Bi Yao is missing, and decide to attack again","Pu Hong tells how Pu Zhi was refused by Qingyun, wounded by a man in black, and taught Xiaofan the Great Brahma Prajna","Pu Zhi, corrupted by the Sinister Bead, massacred Grass Temple Village to force Qingyun to take the boys"],"introduced":["Pu Kong (Tian Yin Temple monk)","Zhu Xian Sword Formation (first used)"],"cultivation":"A demon leader asks whether Dao Xuan has 'mastered the level of Taiqing' (Grand Purity) on seeing the Zhu Xian Sword Formation. The demon camp says wielding the Zhu Xian Sword takes a very high level and that a weaker user is driven mad by it; this formation was 'not even 30%' of its full power.","confidence":"high"},{"ep":26,"title":"Bi Yao's sacrifice","summary":"Learning that Pu Zhi massacred Grass Temple Village, Zhang Xiaofan breaks down. Pu Hong says Pu Zhi was possessed by the Sinister Bead and that Xiaofan is not to blame, but Xiaofan rages that he kept Pu Zhi's secret at the risk of his life and got nothing for it, and attacks. Dao Xuan stops him with 'Seven Stars Return', Bi Yao tries to take him away, and the Ghost King arrives to protect his daughter as the Demon Sect attacks again. Fa Xiang strikes Xiaofan with the Samsara Bead and wounds his heart, and Xiaofan slips into a killing rage until Bi Yao calls him back. Saying Xiaofan has fallen, Dao Xuan brings down the Zhu Xian Sword on him. Bi Yao chants a blood spell, offers herself, and takes the blow in his place. Afterwards Qing Long begs Mr. Ghost to save her: Mr. Ghost explains that the Lovestruck Spell costs the caster any rebirth, that the Hehuan Bell caught her soul and kept her body whole, and that the only hope is a legendary revival spell from the Southern Border. Holding her, Xiaofan tells Bi Yao it was her he saw in the Full Moon Ancient Well. A closing scene jumps ten years ahead.","events":["Xiaofan breaks down at Pu Zhi's crime and turns on everyone","Dao Xuan stops him with 'Seven Stars Return'; Bi Yao tries to take him away","The Ghost King arrives to protect Bi Yao and faces Dao Xuan; the Demon Sect attacks","Fa Xiang wounds Xiaofan with the Samsara Bead; Xiaofan falls into a killing rage","Bi Yao calls Xiaofan back; Dao Xuan strikes at him with the Zhu Xian Sword","Bi Yao casts the Lovestruck Spell and dies in his place","Mr. Ghost says the Hehuan Bell holds her soul; only a Southern Border spell might revive her","Xiaofan tells her he saw her in the Full Moon Ancient Well; ten years later"],"introduced":["Samsara Bead (Fa Xiang's treasure)","Lovestruck Spell (a blood spell that blocks even the Zhu Xian Sword; the caster can never be reborn)","Southern Border (a revival spell said to exist there)"],"confidence":"high"},{"ep":27,"title":"Ten years later: Gui Li","summary":"In a rainy teahouse, Zhou Yixian tells the story of the great war: Zhang Xiaofan's secret came out, the Ghost King attacked Qingyun, and Bi Yao gave her life to shield him. Ten years later Zhang Xiaofan is Gui Li, Vice Master of the Ghost King Sect, and he wipes out the Blood-Refining Hall. Nian Laoda and Lin Feng surrender, but Ye Gou Daoren refuses to betray the hall, so Gui Li spares him and keeps him at his side. Back at the Ghost King Sect, Gui Li sits by Bi Yao's body and tells her about his mission, while Qing Long and Zhu Que warn that the Ghost King's training has not cured his longing for her. The Ghost King, who has taught him two volumes of the Heavenly Book, sends him to the Dead Swamp to strike the Longevity Hall and its master Yu Yangzi, in alliance with the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect and the He Huan Sect, while a treasure is said to be about to appear. On Qingyun, Lin Jingyu leaves the hidden elder who trained him for ten years, and sect leader Dao Xuan reveals he once secretly saved that elder. Dao Xuan sends the young disciples to the western swamp to keep the treasure from the Demon Sect, and Tian Yin Temple and Fen Xiang Valley send disciples too.","events":["Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan in a teahouse; the war and Bi Yao's death are retold","Gui Li destroys the Blood-Refining Hall; Nian Laoda and Lin Feng surrender","Ye Gou Daoren refuses to give in; Gui Li spares him and keeps him by his side","Lu Xueqi calms the angry Water Qilin on Qingyun","Gui Li visits Bi Yao's body; Qing Long and Zhu Que talk about him","Lin Jingyu leaves his hidden master; Dao Xuan speaks with the old elder","The Ghost King sends Gui Li to the Dead Swamp to attack the Longevity Hall","Dao Xuan sends Qingyun's young disciples to the swamp; Fen Xiang's Yan Hong and Li Xun set out"],"introduced":["Gui Li (Zhang Xiaofan's name in the Ghost King Sect)","Yu Yangzi (master of the Longevity Hall)","Dead Swamp (the western swamp)","Longevity Hall","Water Qilin (Qingyun's guardian beast)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":28,"title":"Dawang Village at the edge of the Dead Swamp","summary":"Yu Yangzi, master of the Longevity Hall, kneels before his ancestors and prays that the treasure will restore his failing hall. At Dawang Village, beside the Dead Swamp, Xiao Yicai and the Qingyun disciples arrive to help Fa Xiang drive off Demon Sect fighters. Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan set up a fortune-telling stall; Qin Wuyan of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect poisons Longevity Hall thugs who try to chase them off, then has Xiao Huan read the names Qin and Gui Li. Ye Gou Daoren, angry at his own reading, has his money stolen by the grey monkey Xiao Hui, which gives it to Xiao Huan. Jin Ping'er of the He Huan Sect meets Xiao Huan as an old friend, then joins Gui Li and Qin Wuyan and accuses the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect of killing one of her disciples. In the rain Gui Li gives Xiao Huan his umbrella and insists he is a bad man, then saves her from a fish-man of the Shiwan Mountains. The Longevity Hall reports to Yu Yangzi that the three young masters have taken the bait and entered the swamp without their men.","events":["Yu Yangzi prays to the Longevity Hall's ancestors for the treasure","Xiao Yicai and Qingyun join Fa Xiang against Demon Sect fighters at Dawang Village","Qin Wuyan poisons Longevity Hall thugs and has Xiao Huan read his name and Gui Li's","Xiao Hui steals Ye Gou Daoren's money for Xiao Huan","Jin Ping'er greets Xiao Huan, then meets Gui Li and Qin Wuyan over her poisoned disciple","Gui Li lends Xiao Huan his umbrella and calls himself a bad man","Gui Li saves Xiao Huan from a fish-man; Zhou Yixian explains the Fish-Man Clan","Yu Yangzi learns the three Demon Sect young masters have entered the swamp"],"introduced":["Dawang Village","Qin Wuyan (Ten Thousand Poisons Sect)","Jin Ping'er (He Huan Sect)","Fish-Man Clan (one of the 63 foreign tribes of the Shiwan Mountains)","Poison God (Qin Wuyan's master)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":29,"title":"The night attack on the righteous camp","summary":"Ye Gou Daoren mocks Gui Li for lending his umbrella to the fortune-telling girl and playing the hero, and Gui Li insists he was born a bad man. At the edge of the Dead Swamp the righteous disciples hear cries for help that turn out to be a Demon Sect lure, and Xiao Yicai has them make camp and wait for dawn. Fa Xiang, Li Xun and Lu Xueqi discuss the danger; Xiao Yicai expects Yu Yangzi to strike that night. Yu Yangzi does send the Longevity Hall's main force in a night attack, but the righteous side is waiting in ambush and the hall loses nearly a third of its disciples. Yu Yangzi then comes himself, mocks the young disciples' idea of honour, and traps them in a yin-yang formation. Fa Xiang, Song Daren, Fa Shan and the Qingyun disciples fight back with Taiji Xuanqing techniques and the Golden Body, but his magic weapon grows far stronger inside the formation. The disciples work out that the formation turns yin and yang into the five elements and find its centre, and Lu Xueqi calls down divine thunder with her sword.","events":["Ye Gou Daoren teases Gui Li about the umbrella; Gui Li says he was born a bad man","Cries for help in the swamp turn out to be a Demon Sect lure","Xiao Yicai has the righteous disciples camp at the swamp's edge and expects a night attack","Yu Yangzi orders the Longevity Hall's night attack; the righteous ambush costs him nearly 30% of his disciples","Yu Yangzi attacks in person and traps the disciples in a yin-yang formation","Fa Xiang's Golden Body and the Qingyun disciples' Taiji Xuanqing techniques hold against his magic weapon","The formation's centre is found; Lu Xueqi calls down divine thunder"],"introduced":["Yin-Yang formation (Yu Yangzi's)","Yin Yang Shield","Golden Body Conquers Demons (Fa Xiang's technique)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":30,"title":"The end of Yu Yangzi","summary":"The righteous disciples beat the Longevity Hall at the swamp's edge; Lu Xueqi calls down divine thunder with her sword, and the Longevity Hall flees vowing revenge. Yu Yangzi, weakened after using a Blood Curse to break out, resolves to enter the swamp for the treasure, but that night Qin Wuyan and Jin Ping'er corner him. Jin Ping'er reveals that Yu Yangzi killed her disciple and blamed the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect to set them against each other. Gui Li arrives as well; Yu Yangzi's men surrender, and Yu Yangzi offers to join Gui Li, who refuses, and the old master dies. In the Qingyun camp Wen Min teases Song Daren for being naive, and Xiao Yicai sends a few strong disciples into the poisonous inner swamp. Gui Li leaves Ye Gou Daoren and Sha Sheng to watch the swamp's edge and learns that Qing Long and Zhu Que have secretly come to the Dead Swamp. Xiao Huan returns Gui Li's umbrella, and the disciples enter the poison fog.","events":["Lu Xueqi's divine thunder routs the Longevity Hall","Yu Yangzi, hurt by his Blood Curse, plans to seize the treasure","Qin Wuyan and Jin Ping'er corner Yu Yangzi and expose his plot to set them against each other","Gui Li arrives; the Longevity Hall men surrender and Yu Yangzi dies after Gui Li refuses his offer","Wen Min and Song Daren in the Qingyun camp; Xiao Yicai plans the inner-swamp search","Gui Li posts Ye Gou Daoren and Sha Sheng outside and hears Qing Long and Zhu Que are nearby","Xiao Huan returns Gui Li's umbrella","The righteous disciples enter the poison fog"],"introduced":["Sha Sheng (Gui Li's subordinate)","Meng Ji (a Longevity Hall man)","Blood Curse","Holy Mother Ming Wang (deity of the Demon Sect)"],"cultivation":"Yu Yangzi says his cultivation dropped sharply after using the Blood Curse.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":31,"title":"Lost in the poison fog","summary":"A huge creature in the poison fog scatters the righteous disciples. Xiao Yicai saves a fellow disciple from the swamp's beasts and they push on to find the others. In the fog Gui Li is attacked by a Qingyun swordswoman; after the fight she spares him and warns that next time they meet they will be enemies, and Gui Li asks Xiao Hui why she did not kill him. Fa Xiang, alone, meets Jin Ping'er, who flirts with him; he attacks her as a demoness and she escapes. Zeng Shushu and Lin Jingyu are caught by a carnivorous bladderwort flower, which Zeng Shushu knows how to handle, and Fa Xiang joins them so the three travel on together.","events":["A giant creature scatters the disciples in the fog","Xiao Yicai saves a fellow disciple from swamp beasts","A Qingyun swordswoman fights Gui Li, then spares him with a warning","Gui Li wonders why she let him live","Fa Xiang fights Jin Ping'er, who slips away","Zeng Shushu and Lin Jingyu escape a bladderwort; Fa Xiang joins them"],"introduced":["Bladderwort (a giant insect-eating flower in the swamp)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":32,"title":"Qin Wuyan and the giant ants","summary":"Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan travel on, bickering about money, while Ye Gou Daoren follows them; Xiao Huan is not worried because sister Ping'er gave her a weapon. At night in Fa Xiang's barrier, Lin Jingyu tells Fa Xiang that for ten years he has seen his village's massacre whenever he closes his eyes. Though Zhang Xiaofan is now the feared Vice Master of the Ghost King Sect, Lin Jingyu says he will always count him as his only friend, even if they must fight. Li Xun joins them, pursued by giant ants, and the group of Fa Xiang, Lin Jingyu, Zeng Shushu and Li Xun faces Qin Wuyan, who controls the ants. Fa Xiang urges Qin Wuyan to turn back from the wrong path, and Qin Wuyan asks why the righteous path is the only right one. Outmatched four against one, Qin Wuyan breaks off and flees, swearing to repay Gui Li for an attack, and Li Xun is left poisoned by the ants.","events":["Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan travel, followed by Ye Gou Daoren","Fa Xiang raises a barrier against the swamp's insects","Lin Jingyu tells Fa Xiang that Zhang Xiaofan is still his friend","The group finds signs of a fight and Tian Yin Temple's Buddhist roar","Li Xun arrives chased by giant ants","Fa Xiang, Lin Jingyu, Zeng Shushu and Li Xun fight Qin Wuyan","Qin Wuyan flees, vowing revenge on Gui Li; Li Xun is poisoned"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":33,"title":"Wan Renwang and the fortune-teller","summary":"Jin Ping'er fights Fa Shan of Tian Yin Temple, Xiao Yicai and Yan Hong of Fen Xiang Valley, amused that three sects are after the same artefact. On the road Zhou Yixian meets the Ghost King, an old acquaintance; the Ghost King recalls that Zhou Yixian once read his stars and foretold he would lose his wife and child, which came true. Zhou Yixian confesses he knew nothing of star reading and made it up because the young man was arrogant; the Ghost King tells Xiao Huan to call him Wan Renwang. Qing Long and Zhu Que ask why their arrival is hidden from Gui Li, and the Ghost King says Gui Li mastered the Heavenly Book in ten years instead of thirty. Lu Xueqi meets Gui Li, asks why he risked himself for her at Jade Purity Hall ten years ago, and begs Junior Zhang to come back; he says he has not used that name for a long time and cannot return. Qing Long and Zhu Que plan to trap the Yellow Bird, a Nine Heavens spirit bird expected with the golden light, with the Four Spirits Blood Formation, though Qing Long thinks the formation too cruel and says the Ghost King changed after Bi Yao's death. The disciples find a giant ancient tree whose roots form walls and climb it in search of the relic.","events":["Jin Ping'er fights Fa Shan, Xiao Yicai and Yan Hong","Zhou Yixian meets the Ghost King and admits his old prophecy was made up","The Ghost King tells Xiao Huan his name is Wan Renwang","The Ghost King praises Gui Li's progress with the Heavenly Book","Lu Xueqi asks Gui Li to come back; he says he cannot","Qing Long and Zhu Que discuss capturing the Yellow Bird with the Four Spirits Blood Formation","The disciples find a giant tree with root walls"],"introduced":["Fa Shan (Tian Yin Temple)","Wan Renwang (the Ghost King's name)","Yellow Bird (Nine Heavens Spirit Bird)","Four Spirits Blood Formation","Dragon-trapping pagoda (used by the Ghost King on the Kui Ox at Liubo Mountain)"],"cultivation":"The Ghost King says Gui Li mastered the basics of the Heavenly Book in ten years, where he expected thirty.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":34,"title":"Gui Li against Lin Jingyu","summary":"At the Heavenly King's Treasure Vault, Gui Li wants the artefact inside and Lin Jingyu blocks the way, refusing to let it fall to the Demon Sect. Lin Jingyu asks why Gui Li still uses Qingyun techniques; Gui Li says he uses Qingyun's arts and the Demon Sect's alike to kill. Lin Jingyu says he was the one who lost ten years ago and challenges Gui Li's mix of Buddhist, Taoist and demonic arts, and the two old friends fight with Qingyun spells and Gui Li's blood arts. Gui Li notes that Lin Jingyu reached Upper Purity in only ten years, while Lin Jingyu senses Buddhist power inside Gui Li's Qingyun moves. Jin Ping'er arrives, having held back three righteous disciples, and proposes working with Gui Li for now. Fa Xiang and Zeng Shushu catch up; Zeng Shushu calls Gui Li 'Xiaofan', but Gui Li says his name is Gui Li. The ancient Black Water Serpent rises from below to guard the vault, and Lu Xueqi throws herself in Gui Li's way while Qing Long and Zhu Que prepare their formation nearby.","events":["Lin Jingyu blocks Gui Li at the Heavenly King's Treasure Vault","The two fight with Qingyun spells and blood arts","Gui Li remarks on Lin Jingyu reaching Upper Purity in ten years","Jin Ping'er arrives and allies with Gui Li","Fa Xiang and Zeng Shushu arrive; Gui Li insists on his new name","The Black Water Serpent emerges and attacks","Lu Xueqi risks her life to stop Gui Li","Qing Long and Zhu Que set up their formation"],"introduced":["Heavenly King's Treasure Vault","Black Water Serpent (an ancient demon beast)"],"cultivation":"Gui Li to Lin Jingyu: 'In only ten years you have reached Shangqing' (Upper Purity).","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":35,"title":"The third volume of the Heavenly Book","summary":"The Black Water Serpent's poison is too strong, and Lin Jingyu is hurt as the disciples fall back, unable to get past it to the vault door. Then the Yellow Bird, the legendary Nine Heavens Spirit Bird and the vault's guardian, appears and the two ancient beasts fight. Inside the vault Gui Li wakes beside Lu Xueqi; their wounds have healed, and he tells her she owes him nothing since she came in before the stone door shut. Lu Xueqi refuses to let him take the treasure unless he kills her first. Gui Li finds the third volume of the Heavenly Book, which he can read only because he has studied the first two. Outside, Qing Long and Zhu Que hold their formation and wait for their moment. The episode ends on Xiao Hui doing something unexpected.","events":["Lin Jingyu is wounded by the Black Water Serpent; the disciples retreat","The Yellow Bird appears and fights the Black Water Serpent","Gui Li and Lu Xueqi wake inside the vault, healed","Lu Xueqi tells Gui Li he must kill her to take the treasure","Gui Li finds the third volume of the Heavenly Book","Qing Long and Zhu Que wait in their formation"],"introduced":["Heavenly Book, Volume Three"],"cultivation":"Gui Li reflects that Volume Three of the Heavenly Book cannot be started without the first two.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":36,"title":"The Ghost King at the vault","summary":"Monsters scatter the fighters outside the Heaven Emperor's vault, and the Black Water Serpent withdraws now that the treasure is gone, leaving the Yellow Bird to face Gui Li and Xiao Hui. A Dragon Trap spell and the Dragon-Tamer Cauldron strike, and the Ghost King arrives with his Saint Beast envoys. On the road, Ye Gou Daoren tells Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan that he was born ugly, abandoned and raised by wild dogs, and that the Blood-Refining Hall took him in until Gui Li destroyed it. At the vault the Ghost King leaves the four captured righteous disciples to Gui Li, pointing out that one of them is his childhood friend Lin Jingyu. Gui Li says the Yellow Bird matters more, Qing Long agrees because the Ten Thousand Poisons and He Huan sects are watching, and the Ghost King leaves the matter to him. Lin Jingyu begs Xiaofan to come back to Qingyun, but he answers that his name is Gui Li and he needs no saving, and Fa Xiang decides that pressing him will only push him further. Zeng Shushu says he still sees Gui Li as a friend, holds Xiao Hui once more and gives Gui Li a small gift, and the disciples leave to find the others.","events":["The Black Water Serpent leaves; the Yellow Bird turns on Gui Li and Xiao Hui","The Dragon Trap spell and the Dragon-Tamer Cauldron are used; the Ghost King arrives","Ye Gou Daoren tells Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan his past and the fall of the Blood-Refining Hall","The Ghost King leaves the four righteous disciples, including Lin Jingyu, to Gui Li","Gui Li lets them go to deal with the Yellow Bird; Qing Long backs him and the Ghost King leaves","Lin Jingyu asks Xiaofan to return to Qingyun; he refuses as Gui Li","Zeng Shushu parts from Gui Li as a friend and gives him a gift"],"introduced":["Dragon Trap spell","Dragon-Tamer Cauldron","Ye Gou Daoren's past (raised by wild dogs)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":37,"title":"The Fish-Man Clan and the road to Fen Xiang Valley","summary":"Back at the Ghost King Sect's waystation by the Dead Swamp, Gui Li hears that fish monsters have killed many of his men, that the He Huan Sect was hit too, and that the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect left the swamp overnight. The Ghost King came with two Saint Beast envoys, left the matter to Gui Li and went, so Gui Li sends the troops back to Huqi Mountain and stays to look into the fish monsters. Ye Gou Daoren, who has left the Ghost King Sect after Nian Laoda's betrayal, now travels with Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan. On Qingyun Mountain, Dao Xuan visits Wan Jianyi; they talk about Lin Jingyu and about the Zhu Xian Sword's backlash, which still has not healed after ten years. Jingyu reports that his trip to the Dead Swamp found nothing and says he still respects Cang Song like a father. Gui Li finds Zhou Yixian, who tells him the killers are the Fish-Man Clan of the Shiwan Mountains in the Southern Border, a road guarded by Fen Xiang Valley, so their arrival in force means something is wrong there. Zhou also says the ancient Wu clan's lost texts are most likely held by local cultivation sects in the south.","events":["A subordinate reports the fish-monster attacks; the Ghost King came with two envoys and left everything to Gui Li","Gui Li sends the troops back to Huqi Mountain and stays to investigate","Ye Gou Daoren joins Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan on the road","Dao Xuan and Wan Jianyi talk about Lin Jingyu and the Zhu Xian Sword's backlash; Jingyu reports back and speaks of Cang Song","Xiao Huan meets Gui Li again; he asks Zhou Yixian about the fish monsters","Zhou Yixian names the Fish-Man Clan of the Shiwan Mountains; Gui Li concludes something has happened at Fen Xiang Valley","Zhou says the ancient Wu clan's texts are probably kept by local sects","Jin Ping'er appears; at night Gui Li tells someone calling him 'Junior Zhang' that he cannot go back"],"introduced":["Fish-Man Clan","Shiwan Mountains","Huqi Mountain"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":38,"title":"Fen Xiang Valley's secret deal with the Fish-Man Clan","summary":"Travelling south, Gui Li stops at a tea stall whose owner is closing because monsters have been coming down from the mountains, in land Fen Xiang Valley has always protected. In Fen Xiang Valley, Li Xun learns that Shangguan Ce is interrogating a demon prisoner again. Gui Li spies on a secret meeting between the Fish-Man Clan and a Fen Xiang elder's men: the fish-men complain that the Dead Swamp hunt for the Heaven Emperor's Death Stone failed and cost them many warriors because the valley's information leaked. They agree to find the Death Stone's location within three days, and Gui Li realises the Valley Master himself may be involved. A fish-man spots him and a fight starts; the fish-men present are killed, and Lu Shun's party carries a body back to the valley. Jin Ping'er then reveals she did the killing to avenge both their men, praises Gui Li's Soul-Devouring Stick against her own Purple Light Sword, and offers to help him get into Fen Xiang Valley if he promises not to strike her down without warning as he did Qin Wuyan. That night the two slip into the valley and are spotted.","events":["A tea-stall owner closes up because monsters are attacking people near Fen Xiang land","Shangguan Ce interrogates a demon held for three hundred years; Li Xun visits the valley","Gui Li overhears the Fish-Man Clan and Fen Xiang men discussing the Heaven Emperor's Death Stone","The fish-men agree to report the Death Stone's location in three days; Gui Li suspects the Valley Master","A fight breaks out; the fish-men are killed and their body is taken back to the valley","Jin Ping'er admits she killed them and proposes working with Gui Li","Gui Li and Jin Ping'er sneak into Fen Xiang Valley at night and are discovered"],"introduced":["Shangguan Ce","Lu Shun","Heaven Emperor's Death Stone","Purple Light Sword"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":39,"title":"The golden bells and the Ghost King's plan","summary":"Gui Li and Jin Ping'er are chased through Fen Xiang Valley after golden bells ring an alarm with no wind, and they break out through a mountain pass. Lu Shun, who failed to catch them, wants to report to the Valley Master, but Li Xun says Yun Yilan is in seclusion. The valley's leaders suspect the intruders also killed the Fish-Man chief, regret not getting the Heaven Emperor's Death Stone at the Dead Swamp, and order the disciples to stay inside and strengthen the defences. At Huqi Mountain the Ghost King says the Four Spirits Blood Formation is half complete and needs two more spirit beasts. An envoy he sent to watch Gui Li praises how he handled the Dead Swamp, destroyed Longevity Hall and struck down Qin Wuyan, but confirms he risked his life to save Lu Xueqi from the Black Water Snake. In the valley, Lu Shun ignores Li Xun's order and leads disciples out to catch the intruders, while Gui Li and Jin Ping'er capture a Fen Xiang disciple to question. Two Ghost King Sect members discuss Mr. Ghost, who helped the Ghost King decipher the Dragon-Subduing Cauldron's inscriptions to build the formation.","events":["The golden bells ring; Gui Li and Jin Ping'er escape the chase through a mountain pass","Lu Shun and Li Xun argue about reporting to the secluded Valley Master","Fen Xiang links the intruders to the Fish-Man chief's death and seals the valley","The Ghost King reviews the Four Spirits Blood Formation and hears a report on Gui Li and Lu Xueqi","Lu Shun leads disciples out against orders","Gui Li and Jin Ping'er snatch a Fen Xiang disciple","Ghost King Sect members discuss Mr. Ghost's role in building the formation"],"introduced":["Golden Bell Formation","Four Spirits Blood Formation","Dragon-Subduing Cauldron","Black Water Snake"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":40,"title":"The grey pig and Shangguan Ce","summary":"Gui Li and Jin Ping'er question the captured Fen Xiang disciple. He shows them a Tracking Seal and Illusion Paper Fire, and explains that the valley's Golden Bell Formation relies on a grey pig, a Shiwan Mountains beast with a keen nose that shakes the bells when it smells strangers; he knows nothing about the Fish-Man Clan. Li Xun rebukes Lu Shun for leading disciples out against orders and losing one. Gui Li cooks a rabbit for Jin Ping'er, then turns pale for a moment. That night the valley is thrown into chaos by fighting that Gui Li did not start; Xiao Hui finds the grey pig hiding in a dark alley and draws the disciples away while the fish-men attack and kill Fen Xiang disciples at the gate. Searching the valley's records, Gui Li finds only routine notes and decides the clue to the ancient Wu clan must be kept in some important figure's residence. With the fish-men out of control, the Valley Master sends disciples to ask Shangguan Ce, who has kept away from the world guarding the Mystic Fire Altar for a hundred years, to deal with them, and he comes out.","events":["The captured disciple explains the Tracking Seal, the Illusion Paper Fire and the grey pig behind the Golden Bell Formation","Li Xun rebukes Lu Shun for breaking the stay-inside order","Gui Li cooks a rabbit; Jin Ping'er notices him turn pale","Fighting breaks out in the valley; Gui Li declines Jin Ping'er's suggestion to join in","Xiao Hui finds and leads off the grey pig; fish-men kill disciples at the valley gate","Gui Li searches records for the ancient Wu clan and finds nothing useful","Shangguan Ce leaves the Mystic Fire Altar to deal with the fish-men"],"introduced":["Tracking Seal","Illusion Paper Fire","grey pig","Mystic Fire Altar"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":41,"title":"Inside the Mystic Fire Altar","summary":"With Shangguan Ce away from his post, Gui Li slips into the Mystic Fire forbidden ground, a great altar students may not enter, hoping it holds the ancient Wu clan's texts. The fire power inside is so strong he must resist it at every step, and a red light there carries an evil force almost equal to his Soul-Devouring Stick, nearly taking over his mind. Beneath the altar is an active volcano. Xiao Hui seems to absorb some of the power, and a Crimson Flame Beast, which Gui Li takes for the spirit beast guarding the formation, attacks him. At the valley gate the fish-men attack, and Shangguan Ce arrives and steadies the fight at once; Li Xun says he once cowed sixty-three alien clans. Through an interpreter the fish-men demand the killer of their chief, killed after a secret meeting with Fen Xiang, while Li Xun says a disciple lost control and killed one of them first. Shangguan Ce goes to examine the fish-men's bodies.","events":["Gui Li enters the Mystic Fire forbidden ground and sees the Mystic Fire Mirror's totem","The altar's evil red light nearly overwhelms Gui Li's mind; an active volcano lies below","Xiao Hui appears to absorb the altar's power","The Crimson Flame Beast attacks Gui Li","The fish-men attack the valley gate; Shangguan Ce arrives","The fish-men demand their chief's killer; Li Xun explains how the fighting started","Shangguan Ce examines the bodies"],"introduced":["Crimson Flame Beast","Mystic Fire Mirror"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":42,"title":"Xiao Hui's third eye and the Soul Revival ritual","summary":"In the Mystic Fire Altar, Xiao Hui's third eye opens and it shows itself as a Three-Eyed Spirit Monkey while Gui Li fights the Crimson Flame Beast, which keeps reforming as long as the formation is active. The formation's evil makes the Soul-Devouring Stick harder to control, and Gui Li is flooded by memories of Pu Zhi and of his years on Great Bamboo Peak. At the gate, Shangguan Ce studies the dead fish-men, wonders how such thick-skinned fighters died, and decides the mastermind behind them matters more than they do. He posts red-eyed eagles at every exit, warns that the killer may be disguised among the disciples, and orders Lu Shun to check the Golden Bell Formation and Li Xun to check the disciples, privately fearing a plan centuries in the making is unravelling. Deep in the altar Gui Li finds a cold stone altar carved with ritual images not made by people of the Central Plains, showing Soul Revival Magic, and guesses the Mystic Fire Mirror is the key. A voice in the dark tells him he is not Shangguan Ce, recognises his weapon as made of the Sinister Bead and the Soul-Eating Stick, and warns that its evil has entered his body and will drive him mad.","events":["Xiao Hui opens its third eye as the Three-Eyed Spirit Monkey","The Crimson Flame Beast keeps reforming; the Soul-Devouring Stick's evil surges and Gui Li sees old memories","Shangguan Ce examines the dead fish-men and suspects a hidden mastermind","Red-eyed eagles guard the exits; Lu Shun and Li Xun are ordered to search for the killer","Gui Li finds the cold stone altar and the Soul Revival Magic carvings","A hidden voice confronts Gui Li and warns him about the Soul-Devouring Stick"],"introduced":["Three-Eyed Spirit Monkey","Soul Revival Magic","red-eyed eagles"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":43,"title":"The Nine-Tailed Fox in the Mystic Fire Altar","summary":"The voice belongs to Xiao Bai, a Nine-Tailed Heavenly Fox chained in the depths of the Mystic Fire Altar. She notes that Xiao Hui's third eye has opened but its red light is dimmed by evil power, and that only old Shangguan Ce or the Mystic Fire Mirror could get anyone past the Eight Fiends Formation and its Crimson Flame Beast to the altar's third level. Seeing the mirror on Gui Li, she demands to know what happened to Xiao Liu, the six-tailed fox, who is her son. Gui Li tells her that ten years ago, while he and two friends were investigating trouble at Small Pond Town, Xiao Liu died in the arms of a three-tailed fox and gave him the mirror; he admits his part in the death and offers his life. Xiao Bai spares him and explains the altar is a prison Fen Xiang built for her three hundred years ago, after her fox clan stole the mirror from the valley and only Xiao Liu escaped. Gui Li agrees to put the mirror on the stone altar to drain the Mystic Fire Chains, saying he once watched someone he loved fall to the Zhu Xian Sword. Meanwhile Shangguan Ce finds a faint purple tint on the first dead fish-man's wound, names Jin Ping'er's Purple Light Sword, and the enraged fish-men attack Fen Xiang as the altar begins to erupt.","events":["Xiao Bai reveals herself as the Nine-Tailed Heavenly Fox imprisoned in the altar","She sees the Mystic Fire Mirror and asks after Xiao Liu, her son","Gui Li tells her how Xiao Liu died at Small Pond Town and offers his life","Xiao Bai explains her three-hundred-year imprisonment and the fox clan's theft of the mirror","Gui Li places the mirror on the stone altar to break the Mystic Fire Chains","Shangguan Ce identifies the Purple Light Sword wound and blames Jin Ping'er of the He Huan Sect","The fish-men attack Fen Xiang Valley; the Mystic Fire Altar erupts"],"introduced":["Xiao Bai (Nine-Tailed Heavenly Fox)","Eight Fiends Formation","Mystic Fire Chains"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":44,"title":"Xiao Bai goes free","summary":"The Mystic Fire Altar erupts and Fen Xiang disciples under Li Xun cut down the fish-men at the gate; a disciple who looks like Yan Hong goes off to chase the ones who flee. Freed by Gui Li, Xiao Bai thanks him and Xiao Hui. Gui Li tells her Xiao Liu lies in the deepest part of a cave in a small wood five kilometres from Small Pond Town at Kongsang Mountain, and hands her the Mystic Fire Mirror, which she says is the finest fire treasure of all and, with the Eight Fiends Formation, could destroy the world. Shangguan Ce works out that the 'Yan Hong' who left was Jin Ping'er in disguise and goes to the Valley Master. Yun Yilan orders that Jin Ping'er and the other intruder be caught, saying it is better to kill wrongly than let them escape, and scorns Shangguan Ce for losing the mirror three hundred years ago and now the altar. Xiao Bai gives the mirror back, telling Gui Li it has been holding down the Soul-Devouring Stick's evil and that without it he would have gone mad; he answers that the worst thing in the world is the human heart. Then he asks her whether someone left with only one of the three hun and seven po, body intact but feeling nothing, can be saved, and she says there is a way.","events":["The altar erupts; Li Xun's disciples kill the fish-men; 'Yan Hong' chases the survivors","Xiao Bai is free and wants to visit Xiao Liu; Gui Li tells her where he lies","Gui Li gives Xiao Bai the Mystic Fire Mirror","Shangguan Ce realises 'Yan Hong' was Jin Ping'er in disguise","Yun Yilan scolds Shangguan Ce and orders the intruders caught at any cost","Xiao Bai returns the mirror and warns Gui Li about the Soul-Devouring Stick","Gui Li asks how to save someone with only one soul left; Xiao Bai says there is a way"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":45,"title":"Xiao Bai joins Gui Li; Lu Xueqi is sent south","summary":"Xiao Bai tells Gui Li she once saw Soul Revival Magic used to save a man who had lost one hun and three po, so there is hope for his friend while one soul remains. She means the Black Wu Clan of the Shiwan Mountains, which Gui Li has searched for in vain for ten years; she met them two hundred years before her imprisonment, so they existed at least five hundred years ago, and she offers to lead him to them. She asks him to call her Xiao Bai instead of Senior, and learns the monkey's name is Xiao Hui. Jin Ping'er finds their hiding place, hints that Gui Li caused the volcano's eruption, teases him about Bi Yao and his new companion, and leaves; Fen Xiang disciples arrive soon after, led there by her, and are driven off. On Qingyun Mountain, Dao Xuan says rumours of turmoil in Fen Xiang Valley and trouble for Yun Yilan mean the righteous sects cannot stand by; with Pu Hong of Tian Yin Temple he decides to send disciples, and on Shui Yue's word Lu Xueqi is chosen and told to investigate, not act rashly. At Huqi Mountain the Ghost King hears from Bai Hu about the eruption and decides to let Gui Li stir up Fen Xiang while the Ten Thousand Poisons and He Huan sects wear each other down. Elsewhere Hei Mu, a demon shaman of the ancient Wu clan, says the black fire burns again and the day he waits for is near.","events":["Xiao Bai explains Soul Revival Magic and the Black Wu Clan, and agrees to guide Gui Li","She gives her name as Xiao Bai and meets Xiao Hui properly","Jin Ping'er visits, teases Gui Li about Bi Yao and Xiao Bai, and leaves","Fen Xiang disciples, led there by Jin Ping'er, attack and are driven off","Gui Li notes the Heavenly Book's methods clash with Qingyun's at critical points","Dao Xuan and Shui Yue send Lu Xueqi to Fen Xiang Valley with Tian Yin Temple's disciples","The Ghost King, told of the eruption by Bai Hu, chooses to watch and wait","Hei Mu of the ancient Wu clan says the black fire is burning again"],"introduced":["Black Wu Clan","Hei Mu"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":46,"title":"Fen Xiang Valley burns; south with the fox","summary":"A fire dragon bursts from Fen Xiang Valley as a volcano erupts, wrecking the valley and the spirit veins under it. Frightened townsfolk beg the fortune-teller Zhou Yixian for advice while Fen Xiang disciples close the roads and arrest anyone suspicious. Lu Xueqi arrives on an official visit from Qingyun. Li Xun meets her and puts her up in a village for the night, and talks about the fights they shared at Kongsang Mountain and Liubo Mountain, which she finds odd. Gui Li (Zhang Xiaofan) travels south with Xiao Bai. She tells him her fox clan came from the Southern Border and moved to Huqi Mountain a thousand years ago, where the Ghost King Sect now has its base. That night prisoners escape the valley. Li Xun and Lu Xueqi catch up with Jin Ping'er, who is holding his junior Yan Hong, and Lu Xueqi exposes Jin Ping'er when she disguises herself as him. Three days later Xiao Bai says Tianshui Village is just ahead, with the Golden Clan's Qili Village further south.","events":["The volcano under Fen Xiang Valley erupts and destroys the valley's buildings and spirit veins","Townsfolk turn to Zhou Yixian; Fen Xiang seals the roads and arrests suspects","Li Xun welcomes Lu Xueqi and lodges her in a village; he recalls Kongsang and Liubo","Xiao Bai tells Gui Li the fox clan's history and its link to Huqi Mountain","Gui Li asks about the eruption: someone got into the Fire Altar and used a demonic spell","Prisoners escape; Li Xun confronts Jin Ping'er over Yan Hong","Jin Ping'er's disguise as Li Xun is exposed with Lu Xueqi's help","Three days on, Xiao Bai points the way to Tianshui Village and Qili Village"],"introduced":["Huqi Mountain (home of the Ghost King Sect, named after the foxes)","Tianshui Village","Qili Village (the Golden Clan's settlement)","Golden Clan"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":47,"title":"Tianshui Village and the Red-Eyed Eagle","summary":"A dying man begs the heavens for help, and an unseen voice offers him power if he bows and offers his body and soul to its master. Gui Li and Xiao Bai reach Tianshui Village, which has grown busy in the 300 years Xiao Bai was locked away, and local men fall over themselves to flirt with her. Fen Xiang disciples find Yan Hong hurt and blame Jin Ping'er. Li Xun splits the search, taking the west side and leaving Lu Xueqi the east. At an inn Xiao Bai orders Southern Border dishes and explains each one, and Gui Li quietly reflects that after ten years he finally has a lead on a soul-return technique. Fen Xiang catches up with Jin Ping'er and accuses her of killing one of their disciples. She uses her tricks and a secret message about Qili Cave, and despite the Red-Eyed Eagle tracking her, she gets away.","events":["A desperate man accepts power from a mysterious voice and offers himself to its master","Gui Li and Xiao Bai arrive in Tianshui Village; Xiao Bai is mobbed by admirers","Yan Hong is found hurt; Li Xun and Lu Xueqi split up to trap Jin Ping'er in the village","Xiao Bai orders and explains Southern Border food at an inn","Gui Li's thoughts: ten years of searching, a first clue to soul-return magic","Fen Xiang fights Jin Ping'er over a dead disciple","Jin Ping'er mentions Qili Cave and escapes the Red-Eyed Eagle"],"introduced":["Red-Eyed Eagle (Fen Xiang's tracking bird)","Qili Cave"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":48,"title":"Lu Xueqi's farewell sword dance","summary":"In the Wood Clan, people mock an outcast who came back claiming to be a shaman, but the clan chief has taken him in. The chief's men report that the other three tribes will stay out of their war with the Golden Clan. The sorcerer says a supreme spell taught to him by his master will kill the Golden Clan's Great Shaman and win back their artifact after 200 years. In Tianshui Village, Lu Xueqi asks Gui Li whether he travels with Jin Ping'er. He says no, and she asks him to walk with her. On a hill she admits she lost the Seven Meridians Tournament because he held back, and that he has been on her mind for ten years, since Kongsang Mountain. She says she can never betray Qingyun, so tonight she will cut off ten years of foolish longing: if they meet again, one of them will die. She dances with her sword for him one last time. Xiao Bai watches and says both of them are fools, then she and Gui Li head over Mount Matou towards Qili Village.","events":["The Wood Clan prepares for war with the Golden Clan; the other three tribes agree to stay out","The clan's sorcerer boasts his master's spell will kill the Great Shaman","Lu Xueqi asks Gui Li about Jin Ping'er and asks him to walk with her","She recalls the Seven Meridians Tournament, Kongsang Mountain and Bi Yao's leap in front of the Zhu Xian Sword","She confesses her feelings but says she will never leave Qingyun","She vows that next time one of them will die, then performs a farewell sword dance","Xiao Bai comments on the pair; she and Gui Li cross Mount Matou towards Qili Village"],"introduced":["Wood Clan (Mu tribe)","Bear God (the Wood Clan's deity)","Mount Matou"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":49,"title":"The Great Shaman of the Golden Clan","summary":"Gui Li and Xiao Bai reach Qili Village, which Xiao Bai remembers as violent 300 years ago but which is now peaceful. She says the person she once saw perform a soul-return technique was the Golden Clan's Great Shaman. Xiao Bai points at the sacred altar, which is a grave insult, and villagers try to seize them until the chief, Tu Ma Gu, steps in. Gui Li tells him a friend has lain unconscious for ten years with her soul damaged, and Tu Ma Gu takes the request to the Great Shaman. Meanwhile Xiao Bai drinks the village men under the table. The Great Shaman, who hasn't left the altar in 100 years, agrees to see them when he hears only one soul of three and one spirit of seven remains. Gui Li explains that Bi Yao spent her life blocking the Zhu Xian Sword for him and that a trace of her soul is held in the Hehuan Bell. The Great Shaman says he knows something of the technique but first wants to know who told them about it. At Fen Xiang Valley, Shangguan Ce thanks the Qingyun and Tian Yin guests, says Yun Yilan is in seclusion, and blames the Demon Sect for using the eruption to attack. Lu Xueqi says she and Li Xun heard the demon cultists mention Qili Village, and the guests decide to go and investigate.","events":["Gui Li and Xiao Bai arrive at Qili Village","Xiao Bai offends the altar; Tu Ma Gu stops the villagers from seizing them","Xiao Bai wins a drinking contest with the villagers","The Great Shaman agrees to see them after hearing about the patient's condition","Gui Li tells the Great Shaman how Bi Yao died for him and asks him to save her","The Great Shaman asks who told them about the soul-return technique; the drunk Xiao Bai can't answer","Shangguan Ce blames the Demon Sect for the attack on Fen Xiang; Lu Xueqi brings up the Qili Village lead","Next morning: the Golden Clan's Dog God statue"],"introduced":["Tu Ma Gu (chief of the Golden Clan)","Great Shaman of the Golden Clan","Dog God (the Golden Clan's deity; 'Xiaotian')","soul-return technique"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":50,"title":"The Wood Clan's night raid","summary":"The Wood Clan attacks Qili Village at night to take back the Jade Bone, the holy artifact they say the Golden Clan took from them 200 years ago. Their sorcerer controls wind and clouds in a way that doesn't look like any Central Plains art. The Dog God statue gives the warning that only comes when the clan faces slaughter, so women and children flee to the mountain while the warriors fight. Xiao Bai asks Gui Li if he wants to help. At Fen Xiang, Shangguan Ce sees the evil aura in the sky and rushes ahead, and the guests follow. The sorcerer takes the Jade Bone, the Black Staff, and declares that the Wood Clan will now rule the Southern Border. He says only the Beast Deity can give his clan new life. When Gui Li joins the fight, voices urging him to kill set off a vision of his past: Pu Zhi, Grass Temple Village and the people he lost, and a voice asking whether a few lives aren't worth sacrificing for the greater good. In this frenzy he kills, and a voice keeps telling him 'You killed well' until someone shouts 'Zhang Xiaofan!'","events":["The Wood Clan attacks Qili Village to retake the Jade Bone","The Dog God statue's warning; Golden Clan women and children flee to the mountain","Shangguan Ce sees the evil aura and heads for the fight, with the guests following","The sorcerer seizes the Jade Bone and calls on the Beast Deity","Gui Li joins the fight; chants of 'kill him' trigger visions of Pu Zhi and Grass Temple Village","A voice tells him sacrifice is justified for a great cause; he loses control and kills","Someone shouts his old name, 'Zhang Xiaofan!'"],"introduced":["Jade Bone (the Black Staff Jade Bone, holy artifact of the Southern Border clans)","Beast Deity (named as the Wood Clan's hope)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":51,"title":"Ahetai's betrayal and the righteous sects strike","summary":"Gui Li is caught in a rage, and someone screams that they will kill him. The Wood Clan's own fighters find that their sorcerer Ahetai hasn't handed over the holy artifact as promised and go after him. Ahetai declares the Southern Border is his own, but an envoy of the Beast Deity arrives with an evil dragon, having expected the betrayal, and takes the artifact. Shangguan Ce faces this envoy, an old friend he hasn't seen in 80 years. They speak of a promise made to the Beast Deity together with Yun Yilan, and the envoy leaves. The Fen Xiang disciples, Lu Xueqi and Fa Xiang find Gui Li among dead villagers, women and children included, and attack him. Fa Xiang begs him to let go of his hatred. Gui Li remembers Grass Temple Village, Qingyun, the Seven Meridians Tournament and Lu Xueqi vouching for him with her life, and admits he wants to go back but cannot. Lu Xueqi calls down her Divine Sword Lightning on him.","events":["Gui Li rages and is threatened with death","The Wood Clan learns Ahetai is keeping the holy artifact and turns on him","A Beast Deity envoy with an evil dragon takes the artifact from Ahetai","Shangguan Ce meets the envoy, an old friend from 80 years ago, and lets him go","Li Xun, Lu Xueqi and Fa Xiang accuse Gui Li of slaughtering the villagers and attack","Fa Xiang urges him to let go; Gui Li's memories of Qingyun and Lu Xueqi","Lu Xueqi unleashes her Divine Sword Lightning"],"introduced":["Ahetai (the Wood Clan's sorcerer)","the evil dragon (guardian of the Beast Deity's envoy)","Black Fire (given to Ahetai by the Beast Deity)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":52,"title":"Season 2 finale: the fox's illusion and the Great Shaman's bargain","summary":"Gui Li and Lu Xueqi clash with full force. He tells her he can never go back. As Fen Xiang moves in for the kill, Xiao Bai steps in, mocking the pair for being so tragic, and is recognised as the nine-tailed demon fox. She holds off the Fen Xiang disciples with illusion magic. Fa Xiang uses the Great Brahma Prajna to keep Gui Li from being killed. Lu Xueqi learns that Li Xun struck Gui Li's right shoulder with his jade mallet while he was off guard, and coldly praises his 'technique', while she regrets not arriving sooner to save the burning village. Xiao Bai carries the wounded Gui Li to safety and asks whether he prefers that girl or Bi Yao. He says he owes Bi Yao his life. Shangguan Ce reappears after vanishing for the night and sends everyone back to the valley without explaining. A few days later the Great Shaman, who survived, agrees to try to save Gui Li's friend. In return he asks Gui Li, who holds the Mystic Fire Mirror, to protect the Golden Clan when disaster comes, because their stolen holy artifact is the key to waking the demon king of Southern Border legend.","events":["Gui Li and Lu Xueqi fight; he says he cannot go back","Xiao Bai intervenes and is exposed as the nine-tailed fox; she uses illusion magic","Fa Xiang protects Gui Li with the Great Brahma Prajna","Lu Xueqi confronts Li Xun over his sneak attack with the jade mallet","Xiao Bai tends Gui Li; he says he owes Bi Yao his life","Shangguan Ce returns and orders the Fen Xiang disciples back to the valley","A few days later the Great Shaman agrees to help Bi Yao if Gui Li will protect the Golden Clan","Closing scene: a name card for Qingyunzi, the first-generation sect master"],"introduced":["demon king (Southern Border legend; woken by the holy artifact)","jade mallet (Li Xun's weapon)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":53,"title":"Season 3 begins: Ling Long's seal and the road to Fox Mountain","summary":"In ancient times a demon rose among the hundred thousand mountains and led a beast tide to destroy the human world. The Wu priestess Ling Long gave her own life to power the Eight Ferocious Mystic Fire Formation, sealing the demon in an ancient cave and becoming a stone statue. Before she died, five holy weapons were split among five tribes: as long as they never returned to the cave, the beasts would never rise again. In the present, Gui Li is escorting the Great Shaman to Huqi Mountain under clouds of beast-repelling powder. The Ghost King hears he is bringing a shaman who can heal Bi Yao and goes out with an escort to meet them. At Qili, Lu Xueqi learns from Fa Xiang that the Golden Clan says Gui Li acted to protect them, and decides he is still the Zhang Xiaofan she knew. A Hei Hu who serves the Beast Deity confronts the Great Shaman and calls him a traitor. Wild beasts turned monstrous attack the party, and the Great Shaman is badly hurt, so Gui Li and Xiao Bai fight to get him through. Fa Xiang and Lu Xueqi send word back to their masters, and the Beast Deity's chant shows he has gathered all five holy weapons.","events":["The legend: Ling Long seals the demon with the Eight Ferocious Mystic Fire Formation and turns to stone","The five holy weapons are split among five tribes to keep the seal shut","Gui Li escorts the Great Shaman towards Huqi Mountain; the Ghost King rides out to meet them","Lu Xueqi hears the Golden Clan's account and stops seeing Gui Li as a butcher","The Hei Hu confronts the Great Shaman, who calls him a traitor","Monstrous beasts attack; the Great Shaman is gravely wounded","The Beast Deity chants to break the seal after gathering all five holy weapons"],"introduced":["Ling Long (the ancient Wu priestess)","Eight Ferocious Mystic Fire Formation","five holy weapons","Hei Hu (servant of the Beast Deity)","beast-repelling powder"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":54,"title":"The rite at Huqi Mountain","summary":"Gui Li returns to the Ghost King Sect as its vice sect master, bringing the weakened Great Shaman, who promises to do his best and leave the rest to fate. Xiao Bai meets the Ghost King, who recognises the white fox. Looking at a painting, she tells him she once saved Bi Yao's mother, Xiao Chi, never saw her again before she died, and is glad to help their daughter now. Elsewhere the Beast Deity speaks to the stone statue of Ling Long, saying he cares nothing for the fate of the world and would die if she only asked. At Fen Xiang Valley, Yun Yilan comes out of seclusion, warns that chaos is coming, and leads elite disciples to the Central Plains to meet Qingyun and Tian Yin. In private Shangguan Ce tells him the Beast Deity has broken his seal, which bears on a plan of theirs centuries in the making. The Great Shaman finds that Bi Yao's last consciousness lives in the Hehuan Bell, which guards her. He keeps only Gui Li and the Ghost King with him and begins a formation to draw it out. As the rite peaks, Bi Yao's name is called and Gui Li and the Ghost King cry out 'No'.","events":["Gui Li brings the Great Shaman to the Ghost King Sect","Xiao Bai meets the Ghost King and talks of Bi Yao's mother, Xiao Chi","The Beast Deity speaks to Ling Long's statue","Yun Yilan leaves seclusion and leads Fen Xiang disciples to the Central Plains","Shangguan Ce tells Yun Yilan the Beast Deity has broken his seal","The Great Shaman finds Bi Yao's consciousness in the Hehuan Bell and starts the soul-return rite","The rite reaches its climax; Gui Li and the Ghost King cry out"],"introduced":["Xiao Chi (Bi Yao's late mother)","Yun Yilan (master of Fen Xiang Valley)","Lu Shun"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":55,"title":"After the failed rite","summary":"The rite to restore Bi Yao has failed. Gui Li drinks himself senseless in a tavern, asking whether he can ever go home, and Xiao Huan finds Xiao Hui and then the injured Gui Li; over Zhou Yixian's grumbling she insists on taking him along because he once saved her life. The Ghost King sits by Bi Yao for three days, telling her she is just like her mother. The Great Shaman has died; following a letter Gui Li left, Qing Long is to take his ashes back to the Southern Border, and the Ghost King Sect is to help the tribe there if it is in trouble. Bai Hu reports danger in the Shiwan Mountains, and the Ghost King decides that since Bi Yao is gone, the world will make up for it. On Qingyun, Lu Xueqi reports on her trip, and Dao Xuan and Shui Yue argue over whether Qingyun shares the blame for what Zhang Xiaofan became and whether Xueqi's feelings threaten the sect's name. The Beast Deity, walking through locust-ravaged land, finds an old sword mark and is curious about its lingering hostility. On the road to Qingyun, someone from Gui Li's past attacks him for revenge, and the Beast Deity takes an interest in the fight. Afterwards Gui Li asks what he has done for ten years and what he is living for, and Zhou Yixian tells him that wherever the heart finds peace is home.","events":["Gui Li drinks alone after the failed rite; Xiao Huan and Zhou Yixian take him in","The Ghost King mourns by Bi Yao for three days","The Great Shaman's ashes are to be taken back to the Southern Border by Qing Long, as Gui Li's letter asked","Bai Hu reports danger in the Shiwan Mountains; the Ghost King turns against the world","Lu Xueqi reports to Qingyun; Dao Xuan and Shui Yue argue about Zhang Xiaofan and Xueqi","The Beast Deity examines an old sword mark amid a locust plague","An attacker seeking revenge strikes Gui Li on the road; the Beast Deity watches with interest","Gui Li despairs; Zhou Yixian tells him peace of heart is home"],"introduced":["Heyang City (refugees fleeing to Qingyun Mountain)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":56,"title":"Li Xun's proposal and 'Come away with me'","summary":"Yun Yilan, master of Fen Xiang Valley, comes to Qingyun to warn Dao Xuan about the Beast Deity, and Dao Xuan agrees to write to Abbot Pu Hong so Tian Yin Temple can join a council. Yun Yilan then asks for Lu Xueqi's hand for his disciple Li Xun. Shui Yue agrees, hoping the match will end the rumours about Xueqi and the Demon Sect, but Xueqi refuses in front of everyone. Shui Yue calls her a traitor and has Wen Min take her back to Small Bamboo Peak, where she is confined to the back mountain. Elsewhere Gui Li grills meat and shares it with a stranger who keeps the ancient beast Taotie; they talk about loneliness, and the stranger says the one person he trusted deceived him. Tian Buyi and Su Ru hear of the refused proposal, and Tian Buyi says he would protect Xiaofan even at the cost of his seat. That night Gui Li visits Xueqi, asks her to come away with him to the ends of the earth, and she answers by asking what about Bi Yao.","events":["Yun Yilan warns Dao Xuan about the Beast Deity; Dao Xuan will invite Tian Yin Temple to Qingyun","Yun Yilan proposes a match between Li Xun and Lu Xueqi; Shui Yue agrees","Lu Xueqi refuses in public and is confined to Small Bamboo Peak's back mountain","Gui Li shares roast meat with a stranger and his Taotie; they talk about loneliness and betrayal","Tian Buyi and Su Ru discuss the proposal and Xiaofan","Gui Li visits Xueqi at night and asks her to leave with him","Xueqi asks him: what about Bi Yao?"],"introduced":["Taotie (ancient beast)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":57,"title":"Qing Long's last stand and Cang Song's visit","summary":"The dying Poison God names Qin Wuyan the next head of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect. An urgent message reaches the Ghost King: the beasts of the Southern Border are rising. Pu Hong, Dao Xuan and Yun Yilan meet over the beast tide, which ordinary people cannot resist, and plan to stop it at Luoshen Gate before it reaches the Central Plains. In the Southern Border Qing Long, having led the beasts away from Qilidong, meets Jin Ping'er fleeing the demon kings. The Beast Deity forbids the demon kings to devour one another until his great work is done. Qing Long holds back two demon kings so Jin Ping'er can escape, then fights to the death, and his last message reaches the Ghost King. That night Cang Song, once of Qingyun and now with the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect, comes to the Ghost King Sect as an envoy. Gui Li tests him, using both Taiji Xuanqing and Buddhist techniques, and Cang Song recognises him as Zhang Xiaofan. The Poison God is dead, and Qin Wuyan proposes an alliance of the Ghost King Sect, the He Huan Sect and the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect at Snake Poison Valley. The Ghost King and Gui Li suspect his motives but agree. At the valley Qin Wuyan welcomes the Ghost King and San Miao, and is told Gui Li will bring a gift later. Meanwhile the righteous disciples take up their positions at Luoshen Gate.","events":["The Poison God makes Qin Wuyan head of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect","Pu Hong, Dao Xuan and Yun Yilan plan to stop the beast tide at Luoshen Gate","Qing Long meets Jin Ping'er in the Southern Border; the Beast Deity forbids the demon kings to devour each other","Qing Long covers Jin Ping'er's escape and dies fighting the demon kings","Cang Song visits the Ghost King Sect for the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect and duels Gui Li","News of the Poison God's death and Qing Long's last message; Qin Wuyan proposes an alliance","The three demonic sects gather at Snake Poison Valley; Gui Li's gift is promised","The righteous sects man Luoshen Gate as the beast tide arrives"],"introduced":["Poison God (Qin Wuyan's master, dies)","Cang Song (now with the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect)","Luoshen Gate (the pass into the Central Plains)","Snake Poison Valley","Qilidong (Southern Border)","Poison Blood Flag"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":58,"title":"Chu Wu's soul-thralls and the three-sect alliance","summary":"Gui Li, now Vice Sect Master of the Ghost King Sect, fights the beast Chu Wu with Yan Hui and finds that Qing Long died at its hands. Chu Wu devours souls and binds them as servants, and Qing Long's soul begs Gui Li to free him; Gui Li breaks the beast's thousand shackles and releases the trapped souls. At Snake Poison Valley, Qin Wuyan of the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect shows the Ghost King and Jin Ping'er the sect's ancestral protective formation and the three demonic sects swear an alliance. At Luoshen Gate the righteous sects hold off the beast tide: Li Xun's Fen Xiang disciples, Xiao Yicai, Lin Jingyu, Zeng Shushu, Lu Xueqi and the monks Fa Shan and Fa Xiang fight the demon king Fei, whose poison eats through spells. The beasts suddenly pull back toward the southwest; Xiao Yicai goes to investigate and Li Xun returns to Qingyun to report. At the valley a gift from 'Young Master Blood', a rare demon treasure, is presented to Qin Wuyan, who welcomes Gui Li's arrival.","events":["Gui Li and Yan Hui fight Chu Wu; Gui Li learns Qing Long was killed by it","Qin Wuyan shows the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect's protective formation; the three demonic sects ally","The righteous sects fight the beast tide and the demon king Fei at Luoshen Gate","Qing Long's bound soul asks Gui Li to free him","Gui Li breaks Chu Wu's shackles and releases thousands of souls","The beast tide withdraws southwest; Xiao Yicai investigates, Li Xun reports to Qingyun","A rare demon treasure is presented to Qin Wuyan as Gui Li arrives at Snake Poison Valley"],"introduced":["Chu Wu (soul-devouring beast)","Fei (demon king at Luoshen Gate)","Snake Poison Valley","Luoshen Gate","Ten Thousand Poisons Sect protective formation","Young Master Blood (Gui Li's epithet)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":59,"title":"Qin Wuyan's betrayal and Lu Xueqi against the Evil Dragon","summary":"Following the beast tide southwest, Lu Xueqi saves a mother and child in a ravaged village, and a captured Ghost King Sect disciple admits the sect helped its Vice Sect Master lure the beasts to Snake Poison Valley. At the valley Qin Wuyan suddenly shuts down the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect's protective formation, accusing the Ghost King and San Miao of plotting against him, and leaves the allied sects to the beasts. The legendary beast called the Evil Dragon attacks the village; Lu Xueqi draws it away from the villagers, turns its own lightning against it and kills it with her Divine Sword technique through Tianya. Qin Wuyan kills a disciple who had gone over to the Ghost King Sect and mocks the Ghost King, whom he calls Wan Renwang, for failing to protect his wife and daughter, and San Miao for her greed. He also sneers at Gui Li as an outcast traitor. Then the gift Gui Li gave him, which turns out to be Chu Wu's body, turns against him, the Ghost King praises the show, and Qin Wuyan dies cursing Gui Li.","events":["Lu Xueqi saves villagers; a captured Ghost King Sect disciple says the beasts were lured to Snake Poison Valley","Qin Wuyan disables the protective formation and turns on the Ghost King Sect and the He Huan Sect","The Evil Dragon attacks; Lu Xueqi leads it away from the village","Lu Xueqi turns the dragon's lightning back on it with Tianya and kills it","Qin Wuyan kills a turncoat disciple and mocks Wan Renwang, San Miao and Gui Li","Chu Wu's body, Gui Li's gift, turns against Qin Wuyan","Qin Wuyan dies cursing Gui Li"],"introduced":["Evil Dragon (legendary beast)","Wan Renwang (the Ghost King's name)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":60,"title":"The false Hehuan Bell and the Blood Formation","summary":"As the Ghost King had planned, most of the beasts are drawn off to Qimeng Mountain, and San Miao demands the Hehuan Bell he promised her. The Ghost King hands over the bell, Bi Yao's keepsake. Gui Li, who knows nothing of the plan, fights San Miao and her Eternal Love Threads to keep it, but she gets away with it. The bell is a fake: the Ghost King spent his own lifespan to fill it with poison, and San Miao is struck by a Soul-Absorbing Thorn. He sacrificed half his sect's disciples to wipe out the He Huan Sect and the Ten Thousand Poisons Sect. San Miao turns her deadliest technique on him, but Jin Ping'er, revealed as the Ghost King's hidden agent for twenty years, strikes her down and becomes the new owner of the Purple Light Blade. The Ghost King then readies the Four Spirits Blood Formation, which feeds on the blood of every living thing in Snake Poison Valley. He gives Gui Li fifteen minutes to lead his loyal followers out. Gui Li fights his way back to his men just as the beasts return from Qimeng Mountain. At the end the Beast Deity appears before the Ghost King, asking Ling Long if these are the people she died to protect.","events":["The beasts are diverted to Qimeng Mountain; San Miao claims the Hehuan Bell","Gui Li fights San Miao and Jin Ping'er over the bell; San Miao takes it","The bell is a poisoned fake; the Ghost King's sacrifice and plan are revealed","Jin Ping'er turns on San Miao and takes the Purple Light Blade","The Ghost King prepares the Four Spirits Blood Formation and gives Gui Li fifteen minutes","Gui Li rejoins his followers to break out as the beasts return","The Beast Deity appears before the Ghost King"],"introduced":["Qimeng Mountain","Eternal Love Threads (He Huan Sect technique) and its killing move, Eternal Sorrow Thread","Soul-Absorbing Thorn","Purple Light Blade","Four Spirits Blood Formation"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":61,"title":"Breaking out of Snake Poison Valley","summary":"With the Ghost King's blood formation about to wipe out Snake Poison Valley, Gui Li and his Ghost King Sect followers fight a wounded one-eyed demon king whose poison mist stops victims from gathering mana while it drinks their power to heal. Gui Li strikes the unhealed crack in its eye; the Mystic Fire Mirror activates by itself and lends him the sun's power, and he wonders whether it is linked to the Heavenly Book. He rallies the survivors to cut their way out, but another demon king, Zhu Yan, appears, and the first one rises again, stronger, draining spiritual energy from the blood of the living. Gui Li is hurt and cannot move, his men refuse to leave him, and he holds the demon king back with the Soul-Devouring Stick so they can escape. Lu Xueqi reaches the valley, finds the dead of all three demonic sects, searches for him and finds Gui Li, telling him she will go with him to the ends of the earth. She wakes on Qingyun calling his name. On Qingyun word comes that the Demon Sect was almost wiped out and an item that may be Xiaofan's is brought back, and Tian Buyi speaks to his seventh disciple.","events":["Gui Li and his men fight a poison-draining one-eyed demon king in Snake Poison Valley","The Mystic Fire Mirror activates by itself and helps Gui Li strike the demon king's eye","Gui Li rallies the Ghost King Sect disciples to break out","Zhu Yan appears; the first demon king revives, stronger, feeding on blood","Gui Li, wounded, holds the demon king off with the Soul-Devouring Stick so his men can flee","Lu Xueqi searches the valley and finds Gui Li","Xueqi wakes on Qingyun; news of the Demon Sect's destruction reaches Tian Buyi"],"introduced":["Zhu Yan (demon king)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":62,"title":"Xueqi defies her master as Luoshen Gate falters","summary":"In Yuqing Hall the righteous leaders learn that almost every great name of the Demon Sect died at Snake Poison Valley, and that Lu Xueqi is drained after fighting the Evil Dragon and rushing to the valley. Zeng Shushu and Lin Jingyu are sent with elite disciples to reinforce Luoshen Gate. Gui Li wakes up, rescued by You Ji, who tells him the Sinister Bead's demonic power has reached his heart meridian and that he must find a place strong in Yang and use the Mystic Fire Mirror if he wants to live. He agrees to stay behind and look in on the sleeping Bi Yao every month after the sect moves to a temple in the wilds. Shui Yue confronts Xueqi about Gui Li, whom she names as Zhang Xiaofan. Xueqi swears she will try to kill him with Tianya if they meet, but says she cannot cut the bond, and Shui Yue disowns her. At Luoshen Gate, Lin Jingyu's reinforcements and the Tian Yin monks are nearly overwhelmed by the White Bone Snake Demon and the Shura Bird until the Qingyun elders arrive and cover the retreat to Qingyun.","events":["A demon taunts a Qingyun disciple before Qingyun's swords strike","Yuqing Hall hears the Demon Sect was nearly wiped out; Shushu and Jingyu are sent to Luoshen Gate","You Ji tells Gui Li the Sinister Bead is eating at his heart meridian","Gui Li agrees to stay and watch over Bi Yao after the sect relocates","Shui Yue confronts Xueqi; Xueqi will not give up her love and is disowned","Gui Li leaves with Xiao Hui as Luoshen Gate comes under attack","The White Bone Snake Demon and the Shura Bird break the defence; the elders cover the retreat"],"introduced":["White Bone Snake Demon","Shura Bird"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":63,"title":"Drinks with a stranger and the trap at Heyang City","summary":"Luoshen Gate has fallen and the demon king Fei Yi is devouring the land near Yandang Mountain, so Dao Xuan sends Xiao Yicai, Zeng Shushu and Lu Xueqi with Tian Yin and Fen Xiang disciples to destroy it. Xiao Yicai also carries Dao Xuan's question to Tian Buyi about the Tianji Seal on Great Bamboo Peak's back mountain. Tian Buyi agrees, but warns that lifting the Seven Peaks Tianji Seal will release a thousand years of evil aura and harm whoever wields the Zhu Xian Sword. In an empty town Gui Li drinks again with the stranger he met before. The stranger says the only person he cared about is gone and he must do one last thing for her. In Heyang City, Zhou Yixian, Xiao Huan and Ye Gou Daoren visit the memorial hall where Xiao Huan's father lies, and disturb a Demon Sect master who is gathering dark aura there. He attacks them with crows and corpse puppets. Gui Li steps in to protect the three. The master, also of the Ghost King Sect, asks why he isn't guarding Bi Yao on Huqi Mountain, and the two face off.","events":["News that Luoshen Gate has fallen; Fei Yi is ravaging the land near Yandang Mountain","Dao Xuan sends Xiao Yicai, Zeng Shushu and Lu Xueqi to hunt Fei Yi","Gui Li drinks with the stranger at an inn in an abandoned town","Zhou Yixian, Xiao Huan and Ye Gou Daoren are attacked by crows at a memorial hall","Tian Buyi warns that lifting the Seven Peaks Tianji Seal endangers the Zhu Xian Sword's wielder","A Ghost King Sect master traps the three in Heyang City with corpse puppets","Gui Li intervenes and confronts the master"],"introduced":["Fei Yi (demon king)","Yandang Mountain","Seven Peaks Tianji Seal","Yuelai Inn","Heyang City","Huqi Mountain (where Bi Yao is kept)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":64,"title":"Fei Yi burns in the Red Sea Forest","summary":"Inside the Ghost King Sect master's barrier, Gui Li fights through corpse-puppet doubles and a bone bell while the master tries to take his body and cultivation. Gui Li baits him with his own blood essence, and the master calls the fight a draw, unable to read how strong Gui Li really is. Xiao Yicai, Zeng Shushu, Lu Xueqi, Li Xun and the Tian Yin monks find Fei Yi, an ancient insect demon king that can split into a swarm, and it escapes them. They lure it into the Red Sea Forest, turn the forest into a fire-gathering formation around the Suixin Tree and burn it with Fen Xiang fire. Fei Yi survives by splitting into four insects of earth, water, fire and wind, but the disciples split into four groups and destroy them together. The master tells Gui Li of Huanyue Cave on Qingyun Mountain, where Qingyunzi meditated and the Zhu Xian Sword came from, and Gui Li decides to go there.","events":["Gui Li breaks the master's corpse-puppet doubles and bone bell inside the barrier","Gui Li baits the master with his own blood essence; they call a draw","The disciples fight Fei Yi; it escapes as an insect swarm","Fei Yi is trapped in a fire formation in the Red Sea Forest","Fei Yi splits into four elemental insects; the disciples split into four groups and destroy them","The master says the righteous sects' chances rest on the Zhu Xian Sword Formation","Gui Li resolves to go to Huanyue Cave"],"introduced":["Red Sea Forest","Suixin Tree","Huanyue Cave (Shrine of Ancestors)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":65,"title":"Wan Jianyi at Qingyun's back mountain","summary":"Dao Xuan visits Wan Jianyi at night; the two discuss the Seven Peaks Tianji Seal, and Wan Jianyi warns him of what the Zhu Xian Sword's evil aura will do to its wielder. Zhou Yixian thanks Gui Li for saving them and warns him not to go to Huanyue Cave, because the Soul-Devouring Stick has merged with his blood and is wearing away his mind. Lin Jingyu and Zeng Shushu finish evacuating Heyang City and head back to Qingyun, where Jingyu sees fire on the back mountain. Gui Li slips into Qingyun's forbidden ground and is stopped by an old man, who recognises the Great Brahma Prajna and names him as Zhang Xiaofan, expelled ten years ago. They fight; the old man is impressed that one so young has mastered three great teachings, breaks the stick's demonic power bare-handed, and Gui Li recognises his sword art as that of the legendary Wan Jianyi. Meanwhile the righteous leaders beg Dao Xuan to draw the Zhu Xian Sword as the beasts reach the foot of Qingyun Mountain. Lin Jingyu later finds Wan Jianyi dying. Wan Jianyi asks him about his Dragon-Slaying sword intent, tells him to keep it, and Jingyu swears that Zhang Xiaofan will pay with his life.","events":["Dao Xuan and Wan Jianyi talk about the Seven Peaks Tianji Seal at night","Zhou Yixian warns Gui Li away from Huanyue Cave","Lin Jingyu and Zeng Shushu evacuate Heyang City; Jingyu sees fire on the back mountain","Gui Li enters Qingyun's forbidden ground and fights an old guardian","Gui Li realises the old man is Wan Jianyi","The righteous leaders ask Dao Xuan to draw the Zhu Xian Sword","Lin Jingyu finds Wan Jianyi dying and swears revenge on Zhang Xiaofan"],"introduced":["Qingyun forbidden ground (back mountain)","Slaying Demons and Gods (Wan Jianyi's sword art)","Dragon-Slaying sword intent","Qingyun Giant Tree"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":66,"title":"Dao Xuan's sword intent and Wan Jianyi's last sword","summary":"Gui Li pushes deeper into Qingyun's back mountain, breaking a chain of illusion formations with Taiji arts on his way towards Huanyue Cave. Ancient sword intent guarding the forbidden ground turns on him when it senses his demonic arts, and he realises Dao Xuan left it there many years ago. On the front of the mountain the righteous sects follow Dao Xuan's plan: Tian Yin Temple and Fen Xiang Valley hold the east and west, Dragon Head Peak and Wind Return Peak guard Heyang City, and the other peaks sweep up any demons that slip through. Small Bamboo Peak, with Shui Yue, Lu Xueqi and Wen Min, takes on the White Bone Snake Demon King, which is far stronger than the others, while the elders report other Demon Kings killed. The episode returns to the end of Gui Li's fight with Wan Jianyi. Wan Jianyi strikes with Slaying Demons and Gods, but Gui Li finds the blow was meant to save him: it pulls the Soul-Devouring Stick's backlash out of his body, and Wan Jianyi is left suddenly old. A man who calls Gui Li 'Vice Sect Master' hurries him away as people approach, and Gui Li wonders how he can ever repay the old man.","events":["Gui Li breaks the illusion formations in the back mountain","Sword intent left by Dao Xuan attacks Gui Li for using demonic arts","The righteous sects take up their positions under Dao Xuan's plan","Small Bamboo Peak engages the White Bone Snake Demon King","Wan Jianyi uses Slaying Demons and Gods on Gui Li","The strike draws the Soul-Devouring Stick's backlash out of Gui Li; Wan Jianyi ages","A man calling Gui Li 'Vice Sect Master' takes him away"],"introduced":["White Bone Snake Demon King","illusion formations of the Qingyun forbidden ground","Dao Xuan's guardian sword intent"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":67,"title":"The trial in Huanyue Cave: Gui Li finds his own way","summary":"Inside Huanyue Cave Gui Li meets two figures from Qingyun's past: the Black-Hearted Old Man, first owner of the Sinister Bead, and Daoist Qingye. The two fight with the power of heaven and earth, then turn to Gui Li. Qingye asks what his life would have been if he had kept his heart straight, while the Black-Hearted Old Man tells him the strong prey on the weak and that he should take any power he can use. Meanwhile Small Bamboo Peak's Shui Yue, Wen Min and Lu Xueqi go for the White Bone Snake Demon King's core, and Lu Xueqi finishes it with Tianya. Young Tian Yin monks rescue one of their elders as the Beast Deity appears. Gui Li remembers Tian Buyi telling him, before he was called to the Yuqing Hall over the Fire Stick, that Su Ru's sword Mo Xue was once a Ten Thousand Poisons Sect weapon taken by Wan Jianyi, and that good and evil lie in the heart, not in a weapon or a method. Gui Li rejects both voices and says his way is in his own heart, and the cave's voice calls the result frightening.","events":["Gui Li meets the Black-Hearted Old Man and Daoist Qingye inside Huanyue Cave","The two fight, then each tests Gui Li with his own view of the world","Small Bamboo Peak attacks the White Bone Snake Demon King's core; Lu Xueqi kills it with Tianya","Tian Yin monks rescue an elder as the Beast Deity appears","Gui Li remembers Tian Buyi's words about Mo Xue and about good and evil","Gui Li rejects both the Daoist and the demonic path: 'My way is in my heart'"],"introduced":["Mo Xue (Su Ru's sword, once a Ten Thousand Poisons Sect treasure)","Evil Dragon Covers the Sea (Black-Hearted Old Man's technique)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":68,"title":"The Beast Deity enters the battle; Lin Jingyu breaks with Gui Li","summary":"Gui Li (Zhang Xiaofan) remembers Wan Jianyi's last warning: he left the Tianji Seal on Qingyun's seven peaks, which makes the Zhu Xian Sword's evil aura far stronger but strikes back at whoever starts the formation. Tongtian Peak is the heart of the Sword Formation, and Wan Jianyi had hoped to defuse the seal there with Taiji arts but fell one step short; he thinks Gui Li, who holds the arts of three schools, might finish it. On the front mountain the righteous sects kill the last Demon Kings and report to Dao Xuan. The leaders agree to wear the Beast Deity down first so that Dao Xuan can end him with one stroke of the sword. The Beast Deity then appears, freezes the disciples in place and fuses five Demon Kings into one. Fen Xiang Valley's Sky-Burning Fire and Tian Yin Temple's Buddhist arts strike back, but his demonic rain suppresses everyone's cultivation and the disciples can no longer fly. Meanwhile Lin Jingyu confronts Gui Li about the old man in the Ancestral Hall. Gui Li admits it, saying the old man blocked his way, and Jingyu cuts all ties between them and draws his sword.","events":["Gui Li recalls Wan Jianyi's warning about the Tianji Seal and Tongtian Peak","The Demon Kings are wiped out; the leaders report to Dao Xuan and plan to weaken the Beast Deity before the sword strikes","Xiao Yicai comes to take the younger disciples back to the main peak","The Beast Deity appears, freezes the disciples and fuses five Demon Kings into one","Lin Jingyu asks Gui Li if he caused the old man's death; Gui Li says yes","Tian Yin Temple's Buddhist techniques (Weituo's Descending Wrath, the Ten-Direction Calming Circle) hold the line","The Beast Deity's demonic rain suppresses cultivation and grounds the disciples","Lin Jingyu declares their old bond broken and challenges Gui Li"],"introduced":["Weituo's Descending Wrath (Tian Yin technique)","Ten-Direction Calming Circle (Tian Yin technique)","Sky-Burning Fire (Fen Xiang technique)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":69,"title":"Lin Jingyu's sword; Dao Xuan breaks the Tianji Seal","summary":"Lin Jingyu fights Gui Li, asking why the man he trained day and night to stop had to be his old friend. Between blows he remembers their childhood sparring, when Xiaofan was slow but swore that hard work would carry him. Jingyu uses Wan Jianyi's Qingyun sword technique, Demon and God Slayer, and only breaks through when he remembers Wan Jianyi's lesson that the Dragon Slayer sword must go forward without hesitation. Gui Li asks how Jingyu would feel if the person killed were someone he loved, and Jingyu, shouting for Gui Li to give back his master and his brother Xiaofan, wins; Gui Li tells him to strike, since there is no one left he cares about. On the front mountain the Zhu Xian Sword Formation is raised against the Beast Deity, but the sword cannot reach its full power and the Beast Deity overwhelms Dao Xuan and the leaders. Dao Xuan kneels before the tablet of Ancestor Tiancheng, Qingyun's 17th leader, and confesses that he is breaking a rule and will bear the cost alone. He breaks the Tianji Seal, and the seven peaks pour their power, and the sword's evil aura, into the formation.","events":["Lin Jingyu and Gui Li fight; flashbacks to their childhood sparring","Fen Xiang's Flame Prison and the Zhu Xian Sword Formation strike the Beast Deity","Jingyu uses Demon and God Slayer and recalls Wan Jianyi's lesson on the Dragon Slayer","Jingyu beats Gui Li, demanding back his master and his brother Xiaofan","The Beast Deity overpowers Dao Xuan and the leaders; someone holds him off so the others can flee","Dao Xuan prays before Ancestor Tiancheng's tablet","Dao Xuan breaks the Tianji Seal and the seven peaks feed the Sword Formation"],"introduced":["Ancestor Tiancheng (Qingyun's 17th sect leader, memorial tablet)","Demon and God Slayer (Qingyun sword technique)","Flame Prison (Fen Xiang technique)","Zhongtu (the Beast Deity's name for the Central Plains)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":70,"title":"Dao Xuan against the Beast Deity; Lu Xueqi shields Gui Li","summary":"Gui Li reaches Tongtian Peak, the heart of the Sword Formation that Wan Jianyi told him about. Dao Xuan, with the Tianji Seal open, fights the Beast Deity at the formation's full power, and the Beast Deity says he has finally found an opponent worth fighting. In the Yuqing Hall it is explained that the seal's power is endless but it eats the wielder's life. Dao Xuan wounds the Beast Deity badly and seals the sword's evil aura with his own sword intent, but his life energy runs out and the Beast Deity claims victory. Gui Li puts his grudge with Dao Xuan aside and attacks the Beast Deity, who turns to destroy the Zhu Xian Sword. When Qingyun disciples turn on Gui Li, Lu Xueqi stands in their way and tells him to leave and never come back, and a senior asks whether she means to betray the sect. Qingyun people head into the Huanyue forbidden ground to find the ancient sword, and Great Bamboo Peak's people catch up with Gui Li and recognise him as their seventh disciple.","events":["Gui Li arrives at Tongtian Peak, the heart of the formation","Dao Xuan fights the Beast Deity with the full Zhu Xian Sword Formation","In the Yuqing Hall: the Tianji Seal drains the sword-holder's life","Dao Xuan seals the evil aura and wounds the Beast Deity, then runs out of strength","Gui Li sets aside his grudge and attacks the Beast Deity, who goes after the Zhu Xian Sword","Lu Xueqi shields Gui Li from Qingyun disciples and tells him to leave","Qingyun people enter the Huanyue forbidden ground to find the sword; Great Bamboo Peak finds their seventh disciple"],"introduced":["Heavenly Demon Swallowing the Sun (technique)"],"cultivation":"The Beast Deity says Dao Xuan seems to have the best cultivation foundation in the world.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":71,"title":"The Zhu Xian Sword breaks","summary":"The Zhu Xian Sword starts to slip out of control and its evil aura bursts out, hitting everyone nearby, while Lu Xueqi searches for Gui Li. A stranger breaks into the forbidden ground and wounds Dao Xuan; Tian Buyi drives him off, and the stranger remarks on how far Tian Buyi's cultivation has grown in a hundred years. The stranger tries to tempt Tian Buyi with control of Qingyun and the whole world, but Tian Buyi spits and calls him an evil demon, and he leaves warning that Tian Buyi will regret it. Tian Buyi stays to guard the formation for his senior brother. Badly hurt and holding a damaged sword, Dao Xuan hears a voice urging him to claim a reward from the world and rely on the sword alone; he answers that Qingyun's foundation is people's hearts, not a weapon, and that he will bear the cost alone. Gui Li falls under the sword's evil aura, and Lu Xueqi risks her life to reach him, begging him to wake up and not die like this. Gui Li unites good and evil and his three schools into one, the demonic aura is cleared, and the Zhu Xian Sword is found broken.","events":["The Zhu Xian Sword's evil aura explodes and hits everyone nearby","A stranger wounds Dao Xuan; Tian Buyi drives him off","The stranger tempts Tian Buyi with power over Qingyun; Tian Buyi refuses","Tian Buyi guards the formation while the sect tries to suppress the evil aura","A voice tempts the wounded Dao Xuan; he refuses","Lu Xueqi risks her life to reach Gui Li and wake him","Gui Li unites the three methods; the Zhu Xian Sword is found broken"],"cultivation":"The stranger says Tian Buyi's cultivation has risen greatly in a hundred years.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":72,"title":"The hunt after the battle; strangers carry Gui Li away","summary":"Gui Li hides in the mountain forest with his meridians in chaos and his power nearly spent while Qingyun disciples search for him, among them Zeng Shushu and his father Zeng Shucang. Elsewhere Yun Yilan of Fen Xiang Valley corners the wounded Beast Deity and demands the Eight Mystic Fire Formation, saying the Beast Deity promised it for the five clans' sacred artifacts but handed over only three in hundreds of years. Burning, the Beast Deity remembers Ling Long. The Nine-Tailed Fox Xiao Bai steps in; Yun Yilan recognises her as the thief who stole the Mystic Fire Mirror three hundred years ago, and she says she simply dislikes Fen Xiang Valley. Yun Yilan sends word that Fen Xiang will hunt the demons with all its strength. Zeng Shucang catches the injured Gui Li and plans to take him to Qingyun, but strangers who hide their techniques fight him off and carry Gui Li away. Zeng Shucang judges they are not from the Demon Sect. A Small Bamboo Peak senior scolds Lu Xueqi for helping Gui Li, while Gui Li's rescuers chant sutras and use acupuncture to treat wounds left by the Zhu Xian Sword.","events":["Qingyun disciples, with Zeng Shucang and Zeng Shushu, search the forest for the wounded Gui Li","Yun Yilan corners the Beast Deity and demands the Eight Mystic Fire Formation","Xiao Bai intervenes; Yun Yilan names her the thief of the Mystic Fire Mirror","Fen Xiang Valley vows to hunt the demons","Zeng Shucang captures Gui Li; strangers using a golden-light art rescue him","A Small Bamboo Peak senior rebukes Lu Xueqi","The rescuers treat Gui Li with sutras and acupuncture"],"introduced":["Eight Mystic Fire Formation","the five clans' sacred artifacts"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":73,"title":"Waking in Tian Yin Temple; Pu Zhi waits inside","summary":"Gui Li dreams of his parents naming him Zhang Xiaofan and of Grass Temple Village burning, then wakes in Tian Yin Temple. The monks who rescued him were Fa Xiang and one of his seniors; Gui Li refuses the surname Zhang, and Fa Xiang tells him Abbot Pu Hong will explain why they saved him. A young novice, Faming, brings him honeyed medicine and tells him the temple took him in after he too was rescued. In the Ghost King Sect, the Ghost King learns that Dao Xuan opened the Tianji Seal to win and is badly hurt. A Daoist ally says he has found where every peak's seal lies and that he used the battle to kill a hidden expert on Qingyun's back mountain: Wan Jianyi. The Ghost King promises him Qingyun once the Holy Sect rules the world, and plans to reach some temple ruins in three days. Fa Xiang shows Gui Li the stone steps Pu Zhi spent ten years cutting so ordinary people could climb to the temple, then brings him to Pu Hong. Pu Hong leads him to a hall where Pu Zhi greets him: 'Child, you are finally here.' Gui Li demands what the 247 lives of Grass Temple Village meant to him, and a scene from long ago shows Pu Zhi as a child taken in by Tian Yin Temple and given his name.","events":["Gui Li dreams of his parents and the Grass Temple Village massacre, and wakes in Tian Yin Temple","Fa Xiang tends him; the novice Faming befriends him","The Ghost King hears that Dao Xuan is badly hurt; his Daoist ally says he killed Wan Jianyi","Fa Xiang shows Gui Li the stone steps Pu Zhi carved","Pu Hong brings Gui Li to Pu Zhi, who greets him","Gui Li confronts Pu Zhi over the 247 villagers","A flashback shows Pu Zhi taken in as a child and named"],"introduced":["Faming (young Tian Yin novice)","Pu Fang (strict Tian Yin elder, mentioned)","Pu Zhi's stone steps up to Tian Yin Temple","the Ghost King's Daoist ally"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":74,"title":"Wanye City: Gui Li frees Pu Zhi","summary":"Pu Zhi's past unfolds. He vowed to take the karma of all beings on himself and believed the Sinister Bead could strip that karma away, so he built Wanye City inside himself to hold it. His master warned that karma can only be resolved when Buddhism and Daoism temper each other, and told him never to raise the idea again. The karma broke loose in Grass Temple Village, where Pu Zhi killed the villagers. Gui Li finds himself inside Wanye City with Pu Zhi, who blames himself for the 247 deaths and offers his sinful body to him. Gui Li says killing him a thousand times would not bring the dead back, and Pu Zhi can only apologise. The karma Pu Zhi suppressed rises as a demon and attacks Gui Li. Outside, a full day passes; Fa Xiang begs Pu Hong to help, but Pu Hong says no outsider can reach a mind that hard. Gui Li decides that whether the cause and its fruit were good or evil is his to decide, takes all of it on himself, and the karma dissolves. Pu Zhi attains Buddhahood and is finally at peace, and Gui Li kneels and bows to him as his master.","events":["Pu Zhi vows to bear all beings' karma and builds Wanye City inside himself with the Sinister Bead's help","His master warns only Buddhism and Daoism together can resolve karma","Flashback: the karma takes Pu Zhi over at Grass Temple Village","Gui Li faces Pu Zhi inside Wanye City; Pu Zhi apologises","The suppressed karma attacks Gui Li; Pu Hong refuses to intervene","Gui Li accepts all his karma as his own and it dissolves","Pu Zhi attains Buddhahood; Gui Li bows to him as his master"],"introduced":["Wanye City (the city of karma inside Pu Zhi)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":75,"title":"A blank tablet at Qingyun; the Wordless Jade Wall","summary":"Qingyun holds rites for the disciples who died in the war. Dao Xuan, out of seclusion but not yet healed, places a blank spirit tablet in the Ancestral Hall for an unnamed senior, and insists on it when the elders call it improper. At Tian Yin Temple, Pu Hong warns Gui Li that years of carrying the Sinister Bead have filled him with a backlash that now threatens his life, and offers a way to save him. He takes Gui Li into Mount Sumeru to the Wordless Jade Wall, where Tian Yin's founder, then a wandering monk, sat for three days and nights and understood the Great Brahma Prajna. Gui Li sits beneath the wall while the monks form a Vajra formation around it, saying he still owes Pu Zhi a debt and will try. On Great Bamboo Peak Su Ru has made a new set of clothes for Lao Qi every year for ten years, and Tian Buyi tells her Dao Xuan has grown short-tempered since the war, even scolding Shui Yue; he fears the Zhu Xian Sword's evil aura has got into him. After three days and nights the bead's hostility still fights back, and Pu Hong and his junior debate whether saving Gui Li only helps a future tyrant. A golden light breaks out, someone recalls a prophecy last seen when Qingye came out of seclusion, and Gui Li senses scripture coming from the wall.","events":["Qingyun mourns its dead; Dao Xuan sets a blank spirit tablet in the Ancestral Hall over the elders' objections","Pu Hong offers to save Gui Li from the Sinister Bead's backlash","The story of the Wordless Jade Wall and the Great Brahma Prajna","Gui Li sits under the wall inside the monks' Vajra formation","Su Ru keeps sewing clothes for Lao Qi; Tian Buyi worries about Dao Xuan's temper","After three days the hostility still resists; the monks argue about saving him","A golden light and scripture rise from the Wordless Jade Wall"],"introduced":["Wordless Jade Wall (Tian Yin Temple's treasure, Mount Sumeru)","Mount Sumeru","Vajra formation (Tian Yin)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":76,"title":"Heavenly Book Volume 4 and the lightning tribulation","summary":"Dao Xuan summons Xiao Yicai alone and accuses him of waiting for his master to die so he can take over Qingyun. Xiao Yicai swears before Qingyun's patriarchs that he has never deceived his master, and Dao Xuan backs down, saying he only wants him to stay clear-headed. At the Nether Abyss, the Ghost King Sect reads the storms and strange skies as the sign that the Candle Dragon is being born, and plans to use the abyss's power, with the two spirit beasts held in the Fulong Cauldron as the medium, to catch it. Under the Wordless Jade Wall, Buddhist, Daoist and demonic power fight inside Gui Li until his body can barely hold, and Pu Hong's monks strengthen their Vajra formation. Text appears on the wall, and Pu Hong is stunned to find Heavenly Book Volume 4 in a Buddhist holy place. Gui Li decides that Buddhism asks him to let go, Daoism to follow fate and the demonic path to do as he pleases, but none of them is him, and he will walk his own way. He forces his way past a mysterious seal left by some predecessor, and his cultivation sets off a heavenly lightning tribulation.","events":["Dao Xuan accuses Xiao Yicai of coveting his seat; Xiao Yicai swears loyalty","The Ghost King Sect reads the signs of the Candle Dragon's birth at the Nether Abyss","They plan to catch it using the Fulong Cauldron and its two spirit beasts","The three powers clash in Gui Li under the Wordless Jade Wall","Heavenly Book Volume 4 appears on the wall","Gui Li chooses his own way over Buddhism, Daoism and the demonic path","His breakthrough sets off a heavenly lightning tribulation"],"introduced":["Heavenly Book, Volume 4 (on the Wordless Jade Wall)","Candle Dragon (Zhulong)","Fulong Cauldron","Nether Abyss (Ghost King Sect)"],"cultivation":"Gui Li's cultivation, merged from the Heavenly Book with his Buddhist, Daoist and demonic arts, triggers a heavenly lightning tribulation (852 s). No realm named.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":77,"title":"Gui Li faces the heavenly tribulation alone","summary":"Heavenly punishment lightning falls on Tian Yin Temple. Pu Hong says Gui Li carries on Pu Zhi's line and the monks cannot simply stand aside, but the backlash threatens their own foundations. As Gui Li's power flows out, the monks find their wounds healed, because his Prajna shares a source with theirs. Gui Li thanks them, says heaven is ruthless and only he has anything to lose, and goes to meet the lightning alone. Pu Hong sees Buddhist light, Daoist power and demonic hostility fused in him and thinks he might survive. Nearby, Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan feel the storm and read a hexagram that alarms them. In the Ghost King Sect the Candle Dragon appears; the Ghost King hands its capture to You Ji and his Daoist ally while his own power holds the Kui Ox and Yellow Bird in the Fulong Cauldron, and the beast fights back with a purple blade of light. On Small Bamboo Peak Lu Xueqi, still recovering from her wounds, cannot shake a sense that something has happened. The lightning strips Gui Li of all his cultivation and leaves him with only a mortal body. The monks beg him to run, but he says he has spent half his life running and will end it here, and a third tribulation gathers.","events":["The heavenly lightning tribulation strikes; Pu Hong's monks hesitate to intervene","Gui Li's power heals the monks' wounds","Gui Li chooses to face the tribulation alone","Zhou Yixian and Xiao Huan feel the storm and read an alarming hexagram","The Ghost King Sect fights to capture the Candle Dragon with the Fulong Cauldron","Lu Xueqi feels uneasy while recovering","The lightning destroys Gui Li's cultivation; he refuses to flee","A third tribulation gathers"],"cultivation":"The lightning destroys Gui Li's whole cultivation and leaves him with only a mortal body (464-483 s).","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":78,"title":"The third tribulation; Lu Xueqi sets out (Season 3 finale)","summary":"The third strike of the heavenly tribulation falls. Pu Hong tries to take it on himself, and Fa Xiang rushes to save his master. Stripped of his power, Gui Li sinks towards death, and loving voices call him home, asking whether he has suffered enough. He almost goes, then refuses: he owes too much to the world to give it up, and even if heaven destroys his cultivation and his body, the people in his heart stay. Saying that between heaven and earth he is simply Zhang Xiaofan, he survives with help from a presence he recognises. At Qingyun, Lu Xueqi is charged with letting a demon go for personal feelings and causing the Zhu Xian Sword to break. Her master tells her the story of Tianya, forged 800 years ago from Nine Heavens Mysterious Iron, and says the sword was waiting for her. With the Beast Deity fled badly wounded and Qingyun stretched thin, the leaders agree to send elite disciples to track it, and Lu Xueqi volunteers to make up for her fault; Shui Yue lets her go, telling her to live up to the people and to her sword. At Tian Yin Temple the Wordless Jade Wall is damaged, but Pu Hong says he has no regrets. Gui Li takes his leave, saying he has seen through the world and is still himself, unwilling to let go of the people he cares for.","events":["The third tribulation strikes; Pu Hong tries to shield Gui Li and Fa Xiang tries to save Pu Hong","Near death, Gui Li is called home and refuses to give up","Gui Li survives, declaring he is simply Zhang Xiaofan","Lu Xueqi is charged over the broken Zhu Xian Sword; her master tells her Tianya's history","Qingyun decides to send elite disciples after the wounded Beast Deity; Lu Xueqi volunteers","Shui Yue lets Lu Xueqi go","Gui Li thanks Pu Hong and leaves Tian Yin Temple; the Wordless Jade Wall is damaged"],"introduced":["Nine Heavens Mysterious Iron (Tianya's metal)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":79,"title":"Setting out for the Southern Border","summary":"Life on Great Bamboo Peak has grown lively again since Tian Ling'er's wedding, and Xiao Hui the monkey has come back and is raiding the kitchen with Dahuang. Tian Buyi and Su Ru take the monkey's return as a sign that Zhang Xiaofan still sees the peak as home, even though he survived the Zhu Xian Sword outside Huanyue Cave and now lives as Gui Li. Shui Yue sends Lu Xueqi to the Southern Border with two fellow disciples to hunt the wounded Beast Deity. Gui Li visits the Jin tribe, where the new Great Shaman tells him the Beast Deity cannot be killed, only sealed: its life rests on five divine artifacts, and the Wu priestess once caged it with the Mystic Fire Eight Fiends Formation in the Ancient Demon-Suppressing Cave deep in the Hundred Thousand Mountains. At the ruined Mystic Fire Altar Gui Li finds Xiao Bai waiting for him. In Fen Xiang Valley, Yun Yilan admits to Shangguan Ce and Li Xun that thirty days of summoning the Red Flame beast have failed, and proposes a forbidden method from the Burning Incense Jade Tome: a sacrifice of living human blood. In the Ghost King Sect, three of the Four Spirits have been taken and only the Taotie remains.","events":["Xiao Hui and Dahuang cause chaos on Great Bamboo Peak; Tian Buyi orders the dog made into soup in a fit of temper","Tian Buyi and Su Ru talk about Xiaofan surviving the Zhu Xian Sword and Xiao Hui coming home","Shui Yue sends Lu Xueqi to the Southern Border: 'hold Tianya, do not fail your sword'","Gui Li meets the new Great Shaman of the Jin tribe, who keeps her late master's ashes, sent home by Qingyun","She tells him of the five divine artifacts, the Mystic Fire Eight Fiends Formation and the Ancient Demon-Suppressing Cave","Xiao Bai is waiting for Gui Li at the damaged Mystic Fire Altar","Yun Yilan proposes a living blood sacrifice to restore Fen Xiang Valley's altar formation","The Ghost King Sect has three of the Four Spirits; someone has been sent for the Taotie"],"introduced":["the new Great Shaman of the Jin tribe","five divine artifacts (the Beast Deity's life source)","Mystic Fire Eight Fiends Formation (Xuanhuo Eight Demons Formation)","Ancient Demon-Suppressing Cave, Hundred Thousand Mountains","Red Flame beast / Chiyan Mingzun (Fen Xiang Valley's altar spirit)","Four Spirits (Ghost King Sect plan) and the Taotie"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":80,"title":"Blood on the Mystic Fire Altar","summary":"In Fen Xiang Valley Yun Yilan starts the blood sacrifice, killing his own disciples to feed the altar formation and taunting Shangguan Ce to give his own blood if he objects. Gui Li breaks into the forbidden ground, calls the valley no better than the Demon Sect, and fights Yun Yilan, who is shocked that a man with a few decades of cultivation can match him. The altar erupts in fire and Yun Yilan is wounded; Shangguan Ce orders the matter kept secret, and Li Xun is surprised to find Lu Xueqi there. Gui Li and Xiao Bai escape and head into the Hundred Thousand Mountains toward the Ancient Demon-Suppressing Cave. The Beast Deity tells Xiao Bai that the Wu priestess Ling Long made him from the killing aura of heaven and earth, that she was his whole world, and that she turned cold once he grew as strong as her. On the road Zhou Yixian, Xiao Huan and Ye Gou Daoren help hungry refugees until a monster attacks. Ye Gou Daoren holds it off to save them and the villagers kill it, but he stops breathing, and Xiao Huan refuses to let him go.","events":["Yun Yilan sacrifices Fen Xiang disciples to power the altar formation","Gui Li breaks in and fights Yun Yilan; the Mystic Fire Altar bursts into flame","Shangguan Ce hushes up the incident; Li Xun finds Lu Xueqi in the valley","Gui Li and Xiao Bai head for the Ancient Demon-Suppressing Cave","The Beast Deity tells Xiao Bai he was made by Ling Long and loved her","A monster attacks Zhou Yixian's group; the Five Ghosts charm fails","Ye Gou Daoren saves Xiao Huan and dies; she vows to save him"],"introduced":["Ling Long (Wu priestess) named as the Beast Deity's maker","Hundred Thousand Mountains","Five Ghosts Moving House (Zhou Yixian's escape charm)"],"cultivation":"Yun Yilan, in thought: he has reached the 'Yuyang realm', while Gui Li has cultivated only a few decades.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":81,"title":"Xiao Huan's new master","summary":"Long ago, the young Beast Deity killed villagers who stood in his way and begged Ling Long to forgive him; when she said she would one day die, he asked her to make him human so he could stay with her. In the present Xiao Bai realises he has in fact become human, which is why he was so badly hurt at Qingyun Mountain, and that his deathless body is what kept him from Ling Long. Against Zhou Yixian's warning that it will cost her twenty years of life, Xiao Huan uses the ghost art she taught herself from a well wall as a child, the same art she used to gather Jin Ping'er's scattered soul. A ghostly senior, Mr. Ghost, steps in and saves her and Ye Gou Daoren, takes her as his disciple, gives her a book of his ghost arts and the Blood Jade Bone Shard, and asks that she one day help him save someone. On Tongtian Peak, Tian Buyi, Shui Yue and the other peak masters come to see the ailing Dao Xuan, who accuses them of wanting his seat, says Zeng Shucang hid Cang Song's treachery, and blames Shui Yue for Wan Jianyi's imprisonment and death. Lu Xueqi's party asks Yun Yilan for news of the Beast Deity. In the Hundred Thousand Mountains Gui Li finds his Ghost King Sect subordinate Sha Sheng, half-changed by the blood moon's aura, hides him in a formation and goes on to the Ancient Demon-Suppressing Cave.","events":["Flashback: the Beast Deity begs Ling Long to make him human","Xiao Bai learns the Beast Deity has become human and longs to die","Xiao Huan uses the ghost art to bring Ye Gou Daoren back","Mr. Ghost saves them and takes Xiao Huan as his disciple, giving her the Blood Jade Bone Shard","Dao Xuan turns on the peak masters who come to see him","Lu Xueqi's party asks Yun Yilan about the Beast Deity","Gui Li finds the corrupted Sha Sheng and shields him with a formation"],"introduced":["Blood Jade Bone Shard","ghost art (Xiao Huan's secret technique)","Sha Sheng (Ghost King Sect subordinate; named in EP85)","the blood moon over the Hundred Thousand Mountains","Xiao Mantou (someone Sha Sheng asks Gui Li to visit)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":82,"title":"Hei Hu at the cave mouth","summary":"Gui Li, Xiao Bai and Xiao Hui reach the Ancient Demon-Suppressing Cave, where a statue of Ling Long stands at the entrance. Its fierce guardian spirit attacks them as intruders, until Gui Li names him as Hei Hu, one of the seven warriors who followed Ling Long into the Hundred Thousand Mountains and never came home. Hei Hu admits he was tricked into a great mistake that freed the beast. He says the Beast Deity came back badly hurt, together with the Taotie and another demon of very high cultivation, and thanks Gui Li in Ling Long's name. Xuan Wu and Bai Hu of the Ghost King Sect have orders to capture the Taotie, and plan to strike if Gui Li and the Beast Deity wound each other. They find the hidden Sha Sheng. Lu Xueqi, Zeng Shushu and Li Xun's Fen Xiang disciples follow fresh tracks into the mountains; Wen Min has gone back to Qingyun, and Yun Yilan has let slip a rumour that the Zhu Xian Sword is broken. Lu Xueqi finds a Heavenly Book spell on a body and wonders if Gui Li is here. Hei Hu's brother Hei Mu returns, and Hei Hu blames him for gathering the Five Sacred Treasures and waking the Beast Deity. Hei Mu answers that he did it to keep Ling Long's promise to the beast, and that her other wish was to wipe it out for good.","events":["Gui Li pays respect to Ling Long's statue at the cave mouth","The guardian spirit attacks; Gui Li identifies him as Hei Hu","Hei Hu warns that the Beast Deity returned with the Taotie and a powerful demon","Xuan Wu and Bai Hu plan to take the Taotie and catch Gui Li weakened; they discover Sha Sheng","Lu Xueqi's party hears the Zhu Xian Sword rumour and follows strange tracks","Lu Xueqi senses a Heavenly Book spell and suspects Gui Li is near","Hei Hu confronts Hei Mu over waking the Beast Deity"],"introduced":["Hei Hu (guardian spirit, one of Ling Long's seven warriors)","Hei Mu (Hei Hu's brother)","Ling Long's statue at the cave mouth","Five Sacred Treasures of the Wu clan"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":83,"title":"Face to face with the Beast Deity","summary":"Inside the cave Li Xun catches Jin Ping'er and attacks her to settle her old debt for hurting Yan Hong. Gui Li steps in, and Jin Ping'er notes that his three teachings have grown stronger and fully merged. Xiao Bai explains that, with Fen Xiang Valley's altar ruined, only this cave still holds a complete Mystic Fire Eight Fiends Formation. She also admits the Beast Deity is an old friend, so she will not fight him, but tells Gui Li two things: the beast can be beaten, and in a crisis he should try the Mystic Fire Mirror. Behind the stone door the Beast Deity greets Gui Li as the first to arrive, and they talk about what they want from life. Gui Li says he only ever wanted a simple life, that most of his hardships were not his choice, and that he regrets nothing. He fights because the beast living could cost him people he cares about. Outside, Xiao Bai holds off Li Xun's Fen Xiang disciples so Jin Ping'er can escape. The Beast Deity raises the Eight Fiends Formation and a Red Flame demon with the Fire-Gathering Furnace. Gui Li sees through it as all show and no strength, weaker than the one at Fen Xiang's altar, and then Lu Xueqi arrives.","events":["Li Xun attacks Jin Ping'er over Yan Hong; Gui Li intervenes","Xiao Bai explains the formation and her friendship with the Beast Deity, and points Gui Li to the Mystic Fire Mirror","Gui Li and the Beast Deity talk about regret and why people live","Xiao Bai covers Jin Ping'er's escape from Li Xun's group","The Beast Deity raises the Mystic Fire Eight Fiends Formation and a Red Flame demon with the Fire-Gathering Furnace","Gui Li calls the summoned demon all show; Lu Xueqi arrives"],"introduced":["Fire-Gathering Furnace (Tungku Penampung Api)","Red Flame demon (Monster Iblis Api Merah)"],"cultivation":"Jin Ping'er says Gui Li's three supreme teachings have not only improved but fully merged and no longer clash.","confidence":"medium"},{"ep":84,"title":"The Eight-Direction Fire Dragon","summary":"Before the fight the Beast Deity asks Gui Li and Lu Xueqi for one thing if he loses: to pick a bunch of the lilies Ling Long loved and lay them before her statue at the cave mouth. When Lu Xueqi says she has no greater wish, he says there is still a woman in the world like Ling Long. He drinks with them as with true friends, then shows them the secret of Ling Long's own formation. The Eight-Direction Fire Dragon appears, and Hei Hu remembers Ling Long's dying words that when the dragon came back to this place, all the hatred and karma would end. Gui Li and Lu Xueqi fight side by side, she with the Divine Thunder of the Nine Heavens sword art. The cave starts to fall in. The dying Beast Deity sees Ling Long at last and goes to her, and Hei Hu goes gladly to join his goddess. Elsewhere, someone who had counted on the cave's formation diagram decides to look for surviving Wu clansmen instead. Gui Li and Lu Xueqi rest together, agreeing not to think about tomorrow, and keep the promise of the lilies, though the statue has likely crumbled; they take it that Ling Long has become one with the land she died to protect.","events":["The Beast Deity asks for lilies to be laid before Ling Long's statue if he falls","He drinks with Gui Li and Lu Xueqi before the fight","The Eight-Direction Fire Dragon appears; Hei Hu recalls Ling Long's prophecy","Gui Li and Lu Xueqi fight the Beast Deity; Lu Xueqi uses Divine Thunder","The cave collapses; the Beast Deity dies seeing Ling Long, and Hei Hu passes on","Someone plans to track down Wu clan survivors for the formation's secret","Gui Li and Lu Xueqi rest together and lay the lilies"],"introduced":["Eight-Direction Fire Dragon (Naga Api Delapan Penjuru)","Divine Thunder of the Nine Heavens sword (Lu Xueqi's sword art)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":85,"title":"Gui Li breaks with the Ghost King","summary":"Gui Li finds Sha Sheng killed with ice energy from Ghost King Sect arts and realises Bai Hu did it, on the Ghost King's orders. The Taotie has also been taken: after the Kui Ox of Liubo Mountain and the Yellow Bird of the Dead Swamp, the sect now has three great beasts to power its Blood Formation, and Gui Li heads back to Huqi Mountain. On Great Bamboo Peak Tian Buyi tells Su Ru he must go and see Dao Xuan, who is now ruled by the demon in his heart and has attacked Elder Fan and Xiao Yicai. He admits how much he grieved when Dao Xuan struck his Seventh Disciple with the Zhu Xian Sword ten years ago, but still respects all Dao Xuan has done for Qingyun. At Huqi Mountain Gui Li demands to know whether the Ghost King ordered his men sacrificed at Snake Poison Valley and Sha Sheng killed. The Ghost King offers up the guilty subordinates and kills them himself, and one of his envoys argues that killing such a useful vice master would look bad. Following Xiao Hui into a sealed chamber, Gui Li finds the Four Spirits Blood Formation nearly complete and someone reminds them all that Bi Yao still lies in the ice room. Fearing Qingyun will be the first target, Gui Li decides to warn them, and kills the Ghost King envoy sent to stop him over a ten-year-old grudge. Tian Buyi then walks past the guard into Dao Xuan's hall on Tongtian Peak.","events":["Gui Li finds Sha Sheng killed by Bai Hu's ice; the Taotie is gone","Tian Buyi tells Su Ru he will confront the maddened Dao Xuan","Gui Li questions the Ghost King over the sacrifices at Snake Poison Valley and Sha Sheng's death","The Ghost King has the blamed subordinates killed","Gui Li finds the Four Spirits Blood Formation nearly complete; Bi Yao is remembered","Gui Li resolves to warn Qingyun and kills the envoy who blocks him","Tian Buyi enters Dao Xuan's hall"],"introduced":["Kui Ox of Liubo Mountain, Yellow Bird of the Dead Swamp (two of the Four Spirits)","Snake Poison Valley","Huqi Mountain (Ghost King Sect base)","Four Spirits Blood Formation (Formasi Empat Darah Spiritual)","Elder Fan (Tongtian Peak; mentioned)"],"confidence":"medium"},{"ep":86,"title":"Su Ru storms Tongtian Peak","summary":"The Ghost King hears of Bai Hu's death, and Gui Li is dismissed as a mere boy: in forty-nine days the Dragon-Subduing Cauldron will finish gathering the four spirits and give him the power of the Ming King. The two surviving Saint Beast envoys mourn their fallen brothers and cling to the hope that Bi Yao may still wake. Gui Li kneels at his parents' graves in Grass Temple Village and promises he will not stand by this time. On Small Bamboo Peak, Lu Xueqi has shut herself away since coming home. She tells Wen Min she does not want an immortality without love, and is content to keep one person in her heart knowing she is in his. When Tian Buyi does not come back from Tongtian Peak, Su Ru unseals her sword Moxue and storms the Yuqing Hall, facing down Elders Fan and Yang and Xiao Yicai until Shui Yue arrives. They find the Ancestral Hall wrecked and Lin Jingyu badly hurt but alive, and both Dao Xuan and Tian Buyi gone. Xiao Yicai orders a quiet search, and Su Ru leaves to find her husband herself. Meanwhile Zhou Yixian leads Xiao Huan and Ye Gou Daoren into an old hall of repose, where a man in Qingyun robes vows that anyone who opposes him must die. He is unimpressed by their ghost-moving spell and says such tricks will not save the three of them.","events":["The Ghost King counts down forty-nine days to finishing the Four Spirits formation","The two surviving envoys mourn their dead and hope for Bi Yao","Gui Li visits his parents' graves at Grass Temple Village","Lu Xueqi tells Wen Min she will not give up the man in her heart","Su Ru draws Moxue and storms Tongtian Peak looking for Tian Buyi","The Ancestral Hall is found wrecked: Lin Jingyu is wounded, Dao Xuan and Tian Buyi are missing","Zhou Yixian's group meets a deadly man in Qingyun robes in a hall of repose"],"introduced":["Dragon-Subduing Cauldron (Wadah Penakluk Naga)","Ming King (the power the Ghost King seeks)","Moxue (Su Ru's sealed sword)","Elder Yang (Tongtian Peak)","Yuqing Hall"],"confidence":"medium"}];
